nds):6 +7 =13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3 +2=5 +1=6. Write6, carryover0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4 +3=7. Write7, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):3 +8=11. Wait, hold on. Wait, the first number's millions place: the first number is 673,436,698. Breaking down:.\n\nDigits from right:.\n\nPosition1:8 (units).\n\nPosition2:9 (tens).\n\nPosition3:6 (hundreds).\n\nPosition4:6 (thousands).\n\nPosition5:3 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition6:4 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition7:3 (millions).\n\nPosition8:7 (ten millions).\n\nPosition9:6 (hundred millions).\n\nSimilarly, the second number:538,327,286.\n\nPosition1:6 (units).\n\nPosition2:8 (tens).\n\nPosition3:2 (hundreds).\n\nPosition4:7 (thousands).\n\nPosition5:2 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition6:3 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition7:8 (millions).\n\nPosition8:3 (ten millions).\n\nPosition9:5 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nPosition7 (millions place): first number has 3, second has 8. So 3+8 =11. So write 1 and carryover1.\n\nThen Position8 (ten millions): first has7, second has3. 7+3=10, plus carryover1 is 11. So write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions): first has6, second has5. 6+5=11 plus carryover1 is 12. So write 2 and carryover1. Since there are no more digits, add the 1 in the next position (billions place). So the total becomes 1 2 .. etc.\n\nPutting it all together, the digits from right to left would be:.\n\nPosition1:4.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:3.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:7.\n\nPosition7:1 (from 3+8+ carryover?).\n\nWait, let me retrace step by step:.\n\nLet me do each position step by step carefully.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n1. Units place (position1):.\n\n673436698 has 8 in units.\n\n538327286 has 6 in units.\n\n8 +6 =14. So write down 4, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place (position2):.\n\nFirst number:9, second:8.\n\n9+8 =17, plus carryover1 =18. Write 8, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds place (position3):.\n\nFirst number:6, second:2.\n\n6+2=8, plus carryover1=9. Write9, no carryover.\n\n4. Thousands place (position4):.\n\nFirst number:6, second:7.\n\n6+7=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place (position5):.\n\nFirst number:3, second:2.\n\n3+2=5 +1 (carryover)=6. Write6, no carryover.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place (position6):.\n\nFirst number:4, second:3.\n\n4+3=7. Write7, no carryover.\n\n7. Millions place (position7):.\n\nFirst number:3, second:8.\n\n3+8=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\n8. Ten millions place (position8):.\n\nFirst number:7, second:3.\n\n7+3=10 +1 (carryover)=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place (position9):.\n\nFirst number:6, second:5.\n\n6+5=11 +1 (carryover)=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\n10. Billions place (position10):.\n\nNo digits here except the carryover1. So write1.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left, the digits are:.\n\nPosition1:4.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:3.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:7.\n\nPosition7:1.\n\nPosition8:1.\n\nPosition9:2.\n\nPosition10:1. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
