\n4 (ten millions).\n\n2 (millions).\n\n4 (hundred thousands).\n\n3 (ten thousands).\n\n7 (thousands).\n\n3 (hundreds).\n\n0 (tens).\n\n3 (ones).\n\nSo combining these digits:.\n\n1,4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 3 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
