tarting from the right, the digits we got are 8 (ones), 2 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 6 (ten-thousands), 3 (hundred-thousands), 7 (millions), 9 (ten-millions), 0 (hundred-millions), 6 (billions), and the final carried 1. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any places.\n\nWait, maybe I should do this more systematically, digit by digit from right to left, keeping track of each position.\n\nLet me line them up:.\n\n       833,808,999.\n     +713,552,229.\n     -------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 9 + 9 = 18 → 8, carryover 1.\nTens: 9 + 2 = 11 +1 =12 → 2, carryover1.\nHundreds:9 +2=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\nThousands:8 +2=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\nTen-thousands:0 +5=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\nHundred-thousands:8 +5=13 →3, carryover1.\nMillions:3 +3=6 +1=7 →7, no carryover.\nTen-millions:8 +1=9 →9.\nHundred-millions:3 +7=10 →0, carryover1.\nBillions:8 +7=15 +1 (carryover) =16 →6, carryover1.\nThen the final carryover1 becomes the next digit (10 billions place). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
