t that, but when I first added, I might have made a mistake here. Wait, the ten millions digit for first is 3, second is 2. 3+2=5, no carryover?.\n\nWait but then what about the hundred millions?.\n\nHundred millions:1 +8=9 (no carryover here, since 1+8=9).\n\nWait but earlier when I added the hundred thousands place (8+7+1=16), the carryover 1 went to the millions place. Then millions place was 4 +2 =6 plus 1 is 7. Then ten millions place is 3+2=5. Hundred millions is 1+8=9. So putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits would be:.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nTens:6.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:0 (with a carryover).\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:9. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
