      "text": "1,674,999,210? Wait, let me check that.\n\nWait let me list the digits in order:.\n\nPosition10:1 \u2192 1,000,000,000.\n\nPosition9:6 \u2192 600,000,000.\n\nPosition8:7 \u219270,000,000.\n\nPosition7:4 \u21924,000,000.\n\nPosition6:9 \u2192900,000.\n\nPosition5:9 \u219290,000.\n\nPosition4:9 \u21929,000.\n\nPosition3:2 \u2192200.\n\nPosition2:1 \u219210.\n\nPosition1:0 \u21920.\n\nAdding all those up: 1,600,000,000 +74,000,000 + 999,000 + 210. That's 1,674,000,000 + 999,000 +210 =1,674,999,210.\n\nWait but let me confirm by adding the numbers another way.\n\nAlternatively, adding 877,728,158 + 797,271,052.\n\nLet me do this in parts.\n\nFirst, add 877,728,158 + 700,000,000 =1,577,728,158.\n\nThen add 97,271,052 (since 797,271,052 -700,000,000 =97,271,052).\n\nSo 1,577,728,158 +97,271,052.\n\nAdd 1,577,728,158 +90,000,000 =1,667,728,158.\n\nThen add 7,271,052: 1,667,728,158 +7,271,052.\n\nAdding 7,000,000: 1,674,728,158.\n\nThen add 271,052: 1,674,728,158 +271,052 =1,674,999,210.\n\nYes, that matches. So the correct answer is 1,674,999,210.\n\nWait, but in my initial step-by-step addition I had an error in the thousands place, leading me to an incorrect intermediate step. After correcting that, the final answer is 1,674,999,210.\n\nHmm, so I need to adjust my reasoning accordingly. Let me retrace to ensure all steps are correct now.\n\nRevised step-by-step addition:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n1. Ones: 8 +2 =10 \u21920, carry1.\n\n2. Tens:5+5+1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\n3. Hundreds:1+0+1=2 \u21922, no carry.\n\n4. Thousands:8 (from first number) +1 (second number)=9 \u21929, no carry.\n\n5. Ten thousands:2 +7=9 \u21929, no carry.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7 +2=9 \u21929, no carry.\n\n7. Millions:7 +7=14 \u21924, carry1.\n\n8. Ten millions:7 +9 +1=17 \u21927, carry1.\n\n9. Hundred millions:8 +7 +1=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\n10. Billions: carry1 \u21921.\n\nSo assembling the digits from right to left (positions 1-10):\n\nPositions 1:0, 2:1,3:2,4:9,5:9,6:9,7:4,8:7,9:6,10:1.\n\nTherefore the number is 1 (billions), 6 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),4 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),2 (hundreds),1 (tens),0 (ones). So 1,674,999,210.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,674,999,210. The initial mistake was in the thousands place where I incorrectly added 8 +5 instead of 8 +1. After correcting that, the answer comes out correctly.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 877728158 and 797271052 is \\boxed{1674999210}.\n</think>\n\n",
