 =1,316,624,440\n\nAdd 878,646:\n\n1,316,624,440 +800,000 =1,317,424,440\n\nAdd 78,646:\n\n1,317,424,440 +78,646 =1,317,503,086.\n\nYes, so that matches. So the answer is 1,317,503,086.\n\nWait but in the reasoning steps, when I broke down each digit, I had the same result. So the answer should be correct. Let me check once more using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 522,624,440 + 794,878,646.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n500,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,200,000,000\n\n22,624,440 +94,878,646 = ?\n\n22,624,440 +94,878,646:\n\n22,624,440 +90,000,000 = 112,624,440\n\nAdd 4,878,646:\n\n112,624,440 +4,878,646 = 117,503,086\n\nTotal sum: 1,200,000,000 +117,503,086 =1,317,503,086. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the answer is correct.\n\nSo in the reasoning steps, I need to detail each digit addition step-by-step as per the template. Let me structure the reasoning accordingly.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 0 +6=6.\n\nThen tens:4+4=8.\n\nHundreds:4+6=10, so 0 with carryover 1.\n\nThousands:4+8=12 plus 1 is 13 →3, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:2+7=9 +1=10 →0, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:6+8=14 +1=15 →5, carry1.\n\nMillions:2+4=6 +1=7, no carry.\n\nTen millions:2+9=11 →1, carry1.\n\nHundred millions:5+7=12 +1=13 →3, carry1.\n\nFinally, the carryover 1 becomes the billions place. So the digits are 1 followed by 3, then 1, 7, 5, 0, 3, 0,8,6.\n\nSo putting it all together, the answer is 1,317,503,086.\n']
