(millions), etc. So both numbers are 9 digits. So when adding, we can proceed digit by digit from the right, which is position1 to position9, and carry over as needed.\n\nLet me start over with the addition step by step, digit by digit, keeping track of the carryover.\n\nStarting with position1 (ones):.\n\nNumber1:6, Number2:9. 6 +9 =15. Write down 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\nNumber1:8, Number2:6. 8+6=14. Plus carryover1=15. Write 5, carryover1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\nNumber1:7, Number2:1. 7+1=8. +1=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\nNumber1:4, Number2:3. 4+3=7. +0=7. Write7, carryover0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\nNumber1:2, Number2:7. 2+7=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\nNumber1:4, Number2:8. 4+8=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\nNumber1:9, Number2:2. 9+2=11. +1=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\nNumber1:4, Number2:9. 4+9=13. +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\nNumber1:6, Number2:7. 6+7=13. +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nNow, after all positions, there's a carryover of 1 remaining. So we add a new digit to the left (billions place) which is 1.\n\nPutting all the digits together from last to first (since we started from the right):.\n\nThe digits we wrote, starting from position1 (ones) to position9 (hundred millions), plus the final carryover:.\n\nThe digits from right to left (positions 1 to 9) are:.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nPosition2:5.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:9.\n\nPosition6:2.\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition9:4.\n\nPlus the carryover 1 as the next digit (position10: billions).\n\nSo when written in order from left to right (billions down to ones):.\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I need to arrange the digits properly. Let's see:.\n\nThe final dig