e both numbers vertically aligned by place:\n\n          2 4 5 3 2 6 6 3 9\n\n        + 7 2 2 7 2 4 1 5 0\n\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes:9 +0 =9.\n\nTens:3 +5=8.\n\nHundreds:6 +1=7.\n\nThousands:6 +4=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:2 (from first number) +2 (from second) =4 +1=5.\n\nHundred thousands:3 (first) +7 (second)=10 → write 0, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 (first) +2 (second)=7 +1=8.\n\nTen millions:4 (first) +2 (second)=6 → Wait, hold on. Wait the ten millions place of first number is 4 (since it's 2 (hundred millions),4 (ten millions),5 (millions)...). The second number's ten millions place is 2 (since its digits are 7 (hundred millions),2 (ten millions), 2 (millions)...).\n\nSo ten millions place:4 +2 =6? Wait but earlier I thought it was 4 +7=11, which was wrong. Where did that 7 come from?\n\nWait, this is where the mistake was. In the second number, the ten millions place is 2, not 7. The 7 is in the hundred thousands place. So my earlier calculation was incorrect here.\n\nOh no, that explains the discrepancy. So let's recalculate properly now.\n\nLet me start over with correct digit places.\n\nFirst number (245,326,639):\n\n- Hundred millions:2\n\n- Ten millions:4\n\n- Millions:5\n\n- Hundred thousands:3\n\n- Ten thousands:2\n\n- Thousands:6\n\n- Hundreds:6\n\n- Tens:3\n\n- Ones:9\n\nSecond number (722,724,150):\n\n- Hundred millions:7\n\n- Ten millions:2\n\n- Millions:2\n\n- Hundred thousands:7\n\n- Ten thousands:2\n\n- Thousands:4\n\n- Hundreds:1\n\n- Tens:5\n\n- Ones:0\n\nNow adding each column:\n\nOnes:9 +0=9.\n\nTens:3+5=8.\n\nHundreds:6+1=7.\n\nThousands:6 (first) +4 (second) =10 →0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:2 (first) +2 (second)=4 +1=5.\n\nHundred thousands:3 (first) +7 (second)=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 (first) +2 (second)=7 +1=8.\n\nTen millions:4 (first) +2 (second)=6 → no carryover.\n\nHundred millions:2 (first) +7 (second)=9 → no carryover.\n\nNow, writing the result from