s:5.\n\n- Hundreds:8.\n\n- Tens:6.\n\n- Ones:2.\n\nSecond number 620,274,171:.\n\n- Hundreds millions:6.\n\n- Ten millions:2.\n\n- Millions:0.\n\n- Hundred thousands:2.\n\n- Ten thousands:7.\n\n- Thousands:4.\n\n- Hundreds:1.\n\n- Tens:7.\n\n- Ones:1.\n\nSo adding each column from right to left:.\n\nOnes:2 +1=3.\n\nTens:6+7=13 (write 3, carry 1).\n\nHundreds:8 +1=9 plus the carryover 1? Wait, no. Wait, the hundreds place in first number is 8, second is 1. So 8+1=9, plus carryover 1 makes 10. So 0 and carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: first number's thousands digit is 5, second's is 4. 5+4=9, plus carryover 1 is 10 again. So 0 and carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: first is 7, second is 7 (since ten thousands place in second number is 7). 7+7=14, plus 1 is 15. So 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: first is 4, second is 2. 4+2=6, plus 1 is 7. No carryover.\n\nMillions place: first is 8, second is 0. 8+0=8.\n\nTen millions place: first is7, second is2. 7+2=9.\n\nHundreds millions place:3+6=9.\n\nPutting all together, the digits would be:.\n\nStarting from the right: 3 (ones), then 3 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 9 (hundreds millions). So the number is 998,705,033?.\n\nWait, but let me check again. Let's do it step by step in columns:.\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned:.\n\n          3 7 8 4 7 5 8 6 2.\n\n        + 6 2 0 2 7 4 1 7 1.\n\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n2 +1 =3 → ones place is 3.\n\nTens:6+7=13 → 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:8 +1 (from second number) +1 (carryover)=10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:5 (first) +4 (second) +1 (carryover)=10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carryover)=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +2 +1=7 →7, no carryover.\n\nMillions:8 +0=8.\n\nTen millions:7 +2=9.\n\nHundreds millions:3 +6=9.\n\nSo the result is 998,705,033? Let me confirm by adding the numbers another way,