 carryover1  .\n3. Hundreds:5+0+1=6 →6, no carry  .\n4. Thousands:8+3=11 →1, carryover1  .\n5. Ten-thousands:2+7+1=10 →0, carryover1  .\n6. Hundred-thousands:0+6+1=7 →7  .\n7. Millions:8+0=8 →8  .\n8. Ten-millions:0+9=9 →9  .\n9. Hundred-millions:1+2=3 →3  .\n\nPutting all together: 3 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 5 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is ']]
