erhaps better to think in terms of each digit's position. Let's count from the right:.\n\nNumber 1: 367962176.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 6.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):9.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):6.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3.\n\nSimilarly for the second number: 388451869.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:8.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:5.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition8:8.\n\nPosition9:3.\n\nWait, maybe I should write them vertically aligned properly. Let me do that step by step.\n\nLet me write both numbers with their digits in each place:.\n\nLet me write each digit from right to left (starting with ones place):.\n\nFirst number: 367962176.\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1: 6.\n\nPosition 2:7.\n\nPosition3:1.\n\nPosition4:2.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:9.\n\nPosition7:7.\n\nPosition8:6.\n\nPosition9:3.\n\nSecond number:388451869.\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:8.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:5.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition8:8.\n\nPosition9:3.\n\nNow, adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position1 (ones):.\n\n6 +9 =15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2:7+6=13 +1=14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:1 +8=9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:2+1=3 +1=4. Write4, no carryover.\n\nPosition5:6 +5=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition6:9 +4=13 +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:7 +8=15 +1=16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:6 +8=14 +1=15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nPosition9:3 +3=6 +1=7. Write7, no carryover.\n\nNow, putting all the digits from position9 to position1 (since we built from right to left):.\n\nThe result digits are:.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nPosition8:5.\n\nPosition7:6.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition3:0.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition1:5. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
