) +8 (ten thousands)=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\n5 (hundred thousands) +3 (hundred thousands) +1 =9 (hundred thousands).\n\n5 (millions) +4 (millions) =9 (millions).\n\n3 (ten millions) +8 (ten millions) =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\n8 (hundred millions) +6 (hundred millions) +1 carried =15. So the hundred millions place is 5, and carryover 1 to a new billions place.\n\nWait, but when adding the hundred millions: 8 +6 =14, plus the carried over 1 from the ten millions place? Wait, let me go step by step again carefully.\n\nWait, let me do each digit step by step, perhaps I messed up the positions earlier.\n\nLet me list the digits with their positions:.\n\nFirst number: 835,547,970.\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\n\n2 (tens):7.\n\n3 (hundreds):9.\n\n4 (thousands):7.\n\n5 (ten thousands):4.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\n7 (millions):5.\n\n8 (ten millions):3.\n\n9 (hundred millions):8.\n\nSecond number: 684,380,506.\n\nDigits:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):6.\n\n2 (tens):0.\n\n3 (hundreds):5.\n\n4 (thousands):0.\n\n5 (ten thousands):8.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):3.\n\n7 (millions):4.\n\n8 (ten millions):8.\n\n9 (hundred millions):6.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position 1 (ones):.\n\n0 +6 =6. Write down 6. No carryover.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):.\n\n7 +0 =7. Write 7. No carryover.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\n9 +5 =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\n7 +0 =7 + 1 (carryover) =8. Write 8. No carryover.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n4 +8 =12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n5 +3 =8 +1 (carryover) =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n5 +4 =9. Write 9.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n3 +8 =11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n8 +6 =14 +1 (carryover) =15. So write 5, carryover1.\n\nBut since there's no higher place, we need to add that 1 as a new digit (billions place). So the total sum is 1 (billions) 5 (hundred millions), then the rest.\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nStarting from the highest digit:.\n\n1 (billions), 5 (hundred millions), then the digits from position9 down:.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the digits from highest to lowest:.\n\nAfter adding, the digits are:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nTen millions:1 (from position8's result).\n\nMillions:9.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nHundreds:4.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, maybe I should list all the digits:.\n\nStarting from the billions place:.\n\n1 (from the carryover at hundred millions place addition).\n\nThen the digits from position9 (hundred millions) result:5? Wait no, let me see:.\n\nWait the addition steps:.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8 (from first number) +6 (second) + carryover1 (from ten millions place addition) equals 14 +1? Wait, let's redo that step.\n\nWait, let's go step by step again, more carefully.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1):.\n\nPosition1 (ones):.\n\n0 +6 =6. Sum digit:6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\n7 +0 =7 +0 =7. Sum digit:7, carryover0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\n9 +5 =14. Sum digit:4, carryover1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\n7 +0 =7 +1 (carryover) =8. Sum digit:8, carryover0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n4 +8 =12. Sum digit:2, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n5 +3 =8 +1 (carryover) =9. Sum digit:9, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n5 +4 =9. Sum digit:9, carryover0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n3 +8 =11. Sum digit:1, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n8 +6 =14 +1 (carryover from ten millions) =15. So sum digit here is5, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover after the hundred millions, we need to add a new digit (billions place) with the carryover1.\n\nSo the total sum digits from highest to lowest are:.\n\nBillions place:1,.\n\nHundred millions:5,.\n\nTen millions:1,.\n\nMillions:9,.\n\nHundred thousands:9,.\n\nTen thousands:2,.\n\nThousands:8,.\n\nHundreds:4,.\n\nTens:7,.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nPutting all together, the number is:.\n\n1 (billions),.\n\n5 (hundred millions),.\n\n1 (ten millions),.\n\n9 (millions),.\n\n9 (hundred thousands),.\n\n2 (ten thousands),.\n\n8 (thousands),.\n\n4 (hundreds),.\n\n7 (tens),.\n\n6 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
