      "text": "530,437,352? Wait let me see:\n\nBreaking down each place:\n\n- Hundred millions: 5.\n\n- Ten millions:3.\n\n- Millions:0.\n\n- Hundred thousands:4.\n\n- Ten thousands:3.\n\n- Thousands:7.\n\n- Hundreds:3.\n\n- Tens:5.\n\n- Ones:2.\n\nSo combining those: 530,437,352? Wait let's check again:\n\nWait the millions place is 0, so between hundred millions (5) and hundred thousands (4), there's the millions digit (0). So:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 2 (ones). So written as 530,437,352.\n\nWait, but let me confirm by adding the numbers another way. Let's try adding 207,512,855 and 322,924,497.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made an error in the millions place. Let me add them numerically:\n\n207,512,855.\n\n+322,924,497.\n\nLet me add digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+7=12, so 2 carry1.\n\nTens:5+9=14 +1=15 \u21925 carry1.\n\nHundreds:8+4=12 +1=13 \u21923 carry1.\n\nThousands:2+4=6 +1=7 \u21927 no carry.\n\nTen thousands:1+2=3.\n\nHundred thousands:5+9=14 \u21924 carry1.\n\nMillions:7+2=9 +1=10 \u21920 carry1.\n\nTen millions:0+2=2 +1=3 \u21923.\n\nHundred millions:2+3=5.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left are 2,5,3,7,3,4,0,3,5 \u2192 which is 5,304,373,52? Wait no. Wait arranging properly:\n\nThe digits are:\n\n5 (hundred millions),\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n0 (millions),\n\n4 (hundred thousands),\n\n3 (ten thousands),\n\n7 (thousands),\n\n3 (hundreds),\n\n5 (tens),\n\n2 (ones).\n\nSo that would be 530,437,352. Let me verify with another method. Let's add the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n207,512,855.\n\n+322,924,497.\n\nAdding 200,000,000 + 300,000,000 = 500,000,000.\n\nThen 7,512,855 + 22,924,497.\n\nWait 7,512,855 +22,924,497:\n\n7,512,855 +20,000,000 =27,512,855.\n\nThen add remaining 2,924,497: 27,512,855 +2,924,497 = 30,437,352.\n\nAdding to the 500 million gives 530,437,352. That matches the previous result. So the answer is 530,437,352.\n\nWait but let me check once more. Let me add using another approach:\n\n207,512,855\n\n+322,924,497\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n207,512,855 is 207 million plus 512,855.\n\n322,924,497 is 322 million plus 924,497.\n\nAdding the millions: 207 + 322 = 529 million.\n\nNow add the remaining parts: 512,855 + 924,497.\n\n512,855 + 900,000 = 1,412,855.\n\nThen add 24,497: 1,412,855 +24,497 = 1,437,352.\n\nSo total is 529,000,000 +1,437,352 =530,437,352. Yes, that's the same as before. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 207,512,855 and 322,924,497 is 530,437,352.\n</think>\n\n",
