ion plus 825,930.\n\nAdding the millions: 190 +242 = 432 million.\n\nNow the remaining parts: 924,711 + 825,930.\n\nAdding those:\n\n924,711 + 825,930.\n\nLet's break this down:\n\n900,000 + 800,000 = 1,700,000.\n\n24,711 +25,930 = (24,000 + 25,000) + (711+930) = 49,000 + 1,641 = 50,641.\n\nSo total of the smaller parts:1,700,000 +50,641 =1,750,641.\n\nAdding to the millions: 432,000,000 +1,750,641 =433,750,641. So that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 433,750,641.\n\nWait, but let me try another way, just to be thorough. Maybe using another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\n190,924,711\n\n+242,825,930\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n        1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1\n\n      + 2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0\n\n      -------------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n1st digit (ones): 1 + 0 =1\n\n2nd (tens):1 +3=4\n\n3rd (hundreds):7 +9=16 → 6, carryover 1\n\n4th (thousands):4 +5=9 +1=10 → 0, carryover1\n\n5th (ten thousands):2 +2=4 +1=5 →5\n\n6th (hundred thousands):9 +8=17 →7, carryover1\n\n7th (millions):0 +2=2 +1=3 →3\n\n8th (ten millions):9 +4=13 →3, carryover1\n\n9th (hundred millions):1 +2=3 +1=4 →4\n\nSo combining all digits: 4 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands),6 (hundreds),4 (tens),1 (ones). So 433,750,641. Yep, that matches.\n\nTherefore, the sum is indeed 433,750,641. I think that's correct. I checked it two different ways: breaking into parts and digit-by-digit again. Both give the same result. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 190924711 and 242825930 is \\boxed{433750641}.\n"]
