ition2 (tens):1 (from first) +1 (from second) =2 +1 carried →3, no carry.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1 (first) +4 (second) =5 →5, no carry.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4 (first) +8 (second)=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):5 (first) +4 (second)=9 +1 carried=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2 (first) +2 (second)=4 +1 carried=5 →5, no carry.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7 (first) +1 (second)=8 →8, no carry.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):8 (first) +9 (second)=17 →7, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3 (first) +8 (second)=11 +1 carried=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the final carryover1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:.\n\nPosition1:3.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:5.\n\nPosition4:2.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition8:7.\n\nPosition9:2.\n\nPlus the final carryover1, so the total digits are:. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
