 + 3 = 3, plus the carried 1 makes 4.\n\nHundred millions place: 5 + 8 = 13. So write 3 and carry over 1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover becomes a 1 in the next (billions) place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the ones digit:.\n\nOnes:1, Tens:6, Hundreds:3 (with a carried 1), then thousands:1 (with another carried 1?), wait maybe I need to track each step carefully. Let me go step by step again to avoid mistakes.\n\nLet me list each digit position with their values:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position 1):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 1 + 0 = 1. Sum digit:1. Carryover 0.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 3 + 3 = 6. Sum digit:6. Carryover 0.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):9 +4 =13. Sum digit:3, Carryover 1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4 +6=10 +1(carry)=11. So sum digit is 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1 +0=1 +1(carry)=2. Sum:2, carry 0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):3 +1=4. Sum4, carry0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):9 +7=16. Sum6, carry1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0 +3=3 +1(carry)=4. Sum4, carry0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5 +8=13. Sum3, carry1.\n\nNow, after the hundred millions place, there's a carryover of 1. Since there are no more digits, we add that 1 as the next digit (billions place). So the total sum will have a 1 followed by the digits we've got.\n\nPutting all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits from each position (starting from ones):.\n\nPositions 1-9 and the carryover:.\n\nWait, let me list the digits from the highest to lowest place:.\n\nBillions place: the carried over 1.\n\nHundred millions:3,.\n\nTen millions:4,.\n\nMillions:6,.\n\nHundred thousands:4,.\n\nTen thousands:2,.\n\nThousands:1,.\n\nHundreds:3,.\n\nTens:6,.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nWait, perhaps arranging them properly:.\n\nThe sum is 1 (billions) 3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, but that would be 1,346,241,361? Wait let me check again.\n\nWait, actually when building the number, the digits should be ordered as:.\n\nStarting from the billions place (the carried 1), then hundred millions (3), ten millions (4), millions (6), hundred thousands (4?), wait let me retrace each step:.\n\nWait after each position:.\n\nLet me list each digit's contribution step by step:.\n\nLet me list each position's result:.\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):.\n\n1:1.\n\n2:6.\n\n3:3 (with carryover 1).\n\n4:1 (with carryover1 from previous step?).\n\nWait maybe I need to track each step's result:.\n\nLet me start over, writing down each digit step by step.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically aligned:.\n\n          5 0 9 3 1 4 9 3 1.\n        + 8 3 7 1 0 6 4 3 0.\n        ---------------------.\n\nBut wait, actually, the numbers are:.\n\nFirst number: 509,314,931. Breaking into digits:.\n\nDigits from right to left (positions 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):3.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):9.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):3.\n\nPosition7 (millions):9.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nSecond number:837,106,430. Its digits:.\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:4.\n\nPosition4:6.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition6:1.\n\nPosition7:7.\n\nPosition8:3.\n\nPosition9:8.\n\nSo when adding digit by digit:.\n\nStarting at position1:.\n\n1 (from first) +0 (second) =1. No carryover.\n\nPosition2:3 +3=6. No carry.\n\nPosition3:9+4=13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:4+6=10 +1=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:1+0=1 +1=2. Carryover0.\n\nPosition6:3+1=4. No carry.\n\nPosition7:9+7=16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:0+3=3 +1=4. Carryover0.\n\nPosition9:5+8=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nNow, after position9, there's a carryover1, so that becomes the next digit (the 10th position, which is billions place).\n\nSo the digits from position1 to 10 (including the carryover):.\n\nPosition10:1.\n\nPosition9:3.\n\nPosition8: