 hundred millions place. The first number is 5 and the second is 4. 5 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1 to the next place, which is the billions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits are: 2 (ones), 2 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 4 (ten-thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 5 (ten millions), 0 (hundred millions), and the carried over 1 in the billions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
