ber. So let's recalculate each position with the correct digits.\n\nSo let's redo the digit-by-digit addition properly:\n\nFirst number (529,191,405):\n\nPositions:\n\n0:5\n\n1:0\n\n2:4\n\n3:1\n\n4:9\n\n5:1\n\n6:9\n\n7:2\n\n8:5\n\nSecond number (285,073,331):\n\nPositions:\n\n0:1\n\n1:3\n\n2:3\n\n3:3\n\n4:7\n\n5:0\n\n6:5\n\n7:8\n\n8:2\n\nNow adding each column from position0 to position8, keeping track of carries.\n\nStart with position0 (ones):\n\n5 +1 =6. No carryover. Digit0:6\n\nPosition1 (tens):\n\n0 +3 =3. No carryover. Digit1:3\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):\n\n4 +3 =7. Digit2:7\n\nPosition3 (thousands):\n\n1 +3 =4. Digit3:4\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):\n\n9 +7 =16. Write down 6, carryover 1. Digit4:6, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):\n\n1 (from first number) +0 (second) +1 (carryover)=2. Digit5:2. Carryover 0.\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\n9 +5 =14. Write down4, carryover1. Digit6:4. Carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):\n\n2 +8 =10, plus carryover1 =11. Write down1, carryover1. Digit7:1. Carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):\n\n5 +2 =7, plus carryover1 =8. Digit8:8. No more positions.\n\nSo the digits from position8 to 0 are:\n\n8 (hundred millions),1 (ten millions),4 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),7 (hundreds),3 (tens),6 (ones).\n\nWait, let's list them properly:\n\nPosition8:8\n\nPosition7:1\n\nPosition6:4\n\nPosition5:2\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition2:7\n\nPosition1:3\n\nPosition0:6\n\nSo putting them together: 8 1 4 2 6 4 7 3 6. Wait, let's structure this with commas:\n\nStarting from the left (hundred millions):\n\n8 (hundred millions),\n\nthen 1 (ten millions),\n\nthen 4 (millions),\n\nso 814, then next three digits:\n\n2 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),4 (thousands) → 264,\n\nthen 7 (hundreds),3 (tens),6 (ones) →736.\n\nSo the total is 814,264,736. Which matches the earlier correct total. So my initial mistake was in the breakdown of the second number's thousands place. Now everything