\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 +7=12 +1=13 → digit3, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):4 (from first) +1 (from second) =5 +1 (carryover) =6 → digit6, no carryover?.\n\nWait, the carryover from position6 is 1, so added to the millions place. So yes, 5 in hundred thousands? Wait, let me check again:.\n\nWait, the first number's hundred thousands place is 5 (since breakdown is 924,581,297 → the digits are 9 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), etc. So the hundred thousands digit is 5. The second number's hundred thousands digit is 7 (since 671,789,441 → 6 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),1 (millions),7 (hundred thousands), so yes, 7. So 5+7=12, plus carryover 1 from the ten thousands place (which was 17, so carryover 1). So 12+1=13, so digit3, carryover1 to next (millions place).\n\nThen the millions place: first number has 4 (from 4 in millions place?), and second number has 1 (since 671,789,441's millions digit is 1). So 4 +1 =5, plus the carryover 1 makes 6. So that's digit6, no carryover.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions): first number's ten millions is 2, second's is7. 2+7=9, plus no carryover → 9.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9 +6=15. So digit5, carryover1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover becomes a new digit at the front.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPositions 1-9 digits are:.\n\n8 (ones),3 (tens),7 (hundreds),0 (thousands),7 (ten thousands),3 (hundred thousands),6 (millions),9 (ten millions),5 (hundred millions), plus the final carryover 1 from the hundred millions addition (9+6=15 → 5 and carry 1). So the total digits would be 1 followed by 5,9,6,3,7,0,7,3,8.\n\nWait let me list them step by step:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position 1):.\n\nPosition1:8.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:0.\n\nPosition5:7.\n\nPosition6:3.\n\nPosition7:6.\n\nPosition8:9 (from ten millions: 2+7=9).\n\nPosition9:5 (from hundred millions:9+6=15 → digit5, carryover1)