d), 5 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 4 (ten), 6 (one). The second number is 988,809,292: 9 (hundred million), 8 (ten million), 8 (million), 8 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 9 (ten), 2 (one). .\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places earlier. Let me line them up properly:.\n\nLet's write them vertically:.\n\n        149,125,546.\n      + 988,809,292.\n      ----------------.\n\nBreaking each digit:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6 + 2 = 8.\n\nTens: 4 + 9 = 13 (carry 1).\n\nHundreds: 5 + 2 =7 +1=8.\n\nThousands: 5 +9=14 (carry 1).\n\nTen-thousands: 2 +0=2 +1=3.\n\nHundred-thousands:1 +8=9.\n\nMillions:9 +8=17 (carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:4 +8=12 +1=13 (carry 1).\n\nHundred-millions:1 +9=10 +1=11 (carry 1).\n\nWait, so when adding the hundred-millions place: 1 (from first number) +9 (from second) =10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So that would be 1 in the hundred-millions place and carry over 1 to the billions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:4 (with carryover 1).\n\nTen-thousands:3.\n\nHundred-thousands:9.\n\nMillions:7 (Wait, earlier I had millions as 14, so thousands place is 4, carryover 1. Wait maybe I got confused in the steps. Let me re-calculate step by step carefully.\n\nLet me do this digit by digit systematically. Let's write both numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\nFirst number: 149,125,546.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):.\n\n1 (ones):6.\n\n2 (tens):4.\n\n3 (hundreds):5.\n\n4 (thousands):5.\n\n5 (ten thousands):2.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):1.\n\n7 (millions):9.\n\n8 (ten millions):4.\n\n9 (hundred millions):1.\n\nSecond number: 988,809,292.\n\nBreaking down similarly:.\n\n1 (ones):2.\n\n2 (tens):9.\n\n3 (hundreds):2.\n\n4 (thousands):9.\n\n5 (ten thousands):0.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\n7 (millions):8.\n\n8 (ten millions):8.\n\n9 (hundred millions):9