624,840,318.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\nFirst number: 855,939,091\n\nSecond number:768,901,227\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add 855,939,091 +768,901,227.\n\nBreakdown:\n\nLet me add the millions:\n\n800,000,000 +700,000,000 =1,500,000,000.\n\n55,939,091 +68,901,227.\n\nWait, 55,939,091 +68,901,227:\n\n55,939,091 +68,901,227 = (55,939,091 +60,000,000) +8,901,227 = 115,939,091 +8,901,227 = 124,840,318.\n\nSo total sum is 1,500,000,000 +124,840,318 =1,624,840,318.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the final answer is 1,624,840,318.\n\nWait, but let me check with another approach. Let me add digit by digit again step by step to ensure no miscalculation.\n\nStarting over:\n\nFirst number: 8 5 5 9 3 9 0 9 1.\n\nSecond number:7 6 8 9 0 1 2 2 7.\n\nWait, but actually, when writing them aligned:\n\nFirst number: 8 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions),5 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),0 (hundreds),9 (tens),1 (units).\n\nSecond number:7 (hundred millions),6 (ten millions),8 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),2 (hundreds),2 (tens),7 (units).\n\nWait, perhaps writing vertically:\n\n           8 5 5 9 3 9 0 9 1\n\n         + 7 6 8 9 0 1 2 2 7\n\n        -------------------------\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n1 +7 =8 (no carryover).\n\nNext column (tens):9 +2=11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nNext (hundreds):0 +2=2 +1=3, carryover0.\n\nThousands:9 +1=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:3 +0=3 +1=4, carryover0.\n\nHundred thousands:9 +9=18. Write8, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 +8=13 +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:5 +6=11 +1=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:8 +7=15 +1=16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nNow, the carryover1 is added as a new digit at the beginning, so total is 1 6 2 4 8 4 0 3 1 8.\n\nWait, so the sum is 1,624,840,318. Yes, same as before. Therefore, the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 855,939,091 and 