+9=15 plus 1 →16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we have a carryover of 1 after the highest digit (hundred millions place), we need to add a new digit at the beginning (billions place). So the final digit is 1 followed by the 6 we wrote earlier?.\n\nWait, let me track the carryover again step by step:.\n\nAfter position8 (hundred millions):.\n\n6+9+1 (carryover) =16. So the digit here is 6, and carryover 1.\n\nSince there are no more digits left, the carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the next position (billions place). So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we have so far.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left (positions 0 to 8 plus the carryover) would be:.\n\nPositions:.\n\nAfter all positions:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position0):.\n\n7 (units).\n\n9 (tens).\n\n4 (hundreds).\n\n8 (thousands).\n\n5 (ten thousands).\n\n6 (hundred thousands).\n\n1 (millions).\n\n6 (ten millions).\n\n6 (hundred millions).\n\nplus the carryover 1 at the billions place.\n\nSo the total digits are 10 digits now. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
