r: 691,814,791.\n\nSecond number: 927,053,039.\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with the larger place values:\n\nBillions: 6 +9 =15. But since each is in the hundred millions place, actually, their sum in the hundred millions place is 600,000,000 + 900,000,000 =1,500,000,000. But when adding the numbers, the total is over 1 billion, so the carryover makes sense.\n\nWait, but actually, the first number is 691 million, the second is 927 million. Adding those gives 1,618 million, which is 1.618 billion. Then the rest as before. So all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident the answer is correct.\n\nThus, the final sum is 1,618,867,830.\n']
