nPosition3 (hundreds):5.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\nPosition7 (millions):6.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):4.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):6.\n\nSimilarly, Number2: 814304008.\n\nDigits:.\n\nPosition1:8 (ones).\n\nPosition2:0 (tens).\n\nPosition3:0 (hundreds).\n\nPosition4:4 (thousands).\n\nPosition5:0 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition6:3 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition7:4 (millions).\n\nPosition8:1 (ten millions).\n\nPosition9:8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, that's better. Let me confirm:.\n\nNumber2: 814,304,008.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nDigit 1:8 (ones place).\n\nDigit2:0 (tens).\n\nDigit3:0 (hundreds).\n\nDigit4:4 (thousands).\n\nDigit5:0 (ten thousands).\n\nDigit6:3 (hundred thousands).\n\nDigit7:4 (millions).\n\nDigit8:1 (ten millions).\n\nDigit9:8 (hundred millions).\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nNow let's add digit by digit, starting from position1:.\n\nPosition1: 8 +8 =16 → write 6, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2:2 +0 +1 (carry) =3 → no carryover.\n\nPosition3:5 +0 =5 → no carryover.\n\nPosition4:4 (from Number1) +4 (from Number2) =8 → no carryover.\n\nPosition5:2 +0 =2 → no carryover.\n\nPosition6:8 (Number1) +3 (Number2) =11 → write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:6 (Number1) +4 (Number2) +1 (carry) =11 → write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:4 (Number1) +1 (Number2) +1 (carry) =6 → no carryover?.\n\nWait, 4+1 is 5, plus 1 is 6. So write 6, no carryover.\n\nPosition9:6 (Number1) +8 (Number2) =14 → write 4 and carryover1. But since this is the highest digit, we need to add that carryover as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nWait, so after adding position9 (hundred millions place), which gives 6+8=14, plus any carryover? Wait, let's retrace:.\n\nWait, after Position8 (ten millions place):.\n\nPosition8 digits: 4 (Number1) and1 (Number2), plus the carryover from Position7.\n\nWait, let's go step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from Position1 to Position9:.\n\n1. Position1 (ones)