\n- 2 (tens).\n- 6 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 805,280,380.\nBreaking down:.\n- 8 (hundred millions).\n- 0 (ten millions).\n- 5 (millions).\n- 2 (hundred thousands).\n- 8 (ten thousands).\n- 0 (thousands).\n- 3 (hundreds).\n- 8 (tens).\n- 0 (ones).\n\nHmm, perhaps aligning them vertically by place:.\n\n        1 7 1 9 3 9 5 2 6.\n      + 8 0 5 2 8 0 3 8 0.\n      --------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 6 + 0 = 6. Write 6.\n\nTens: 2 + 8 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 3 = 8, plus 1 carried over = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 9 + 0 = 9. Write 9.\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 8 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 9 + 2 = 11, plus 1 carried over = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: 1 + 5 = 6, plus 1 carried over = 7. Write 7.\n\nTen millions: 7 + 0 =7. Write 7.\n\nHundred millions: 1 +8 =9. Write 9.\n\nWait, let me check each step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 6 + 0 = 6. Correct.\n\n2. Tens: 2 +8 =10. So 0 with carryover 1. Correct.\n\n3. Hundreds: 5 +3 =8 plus 1 is 9. Correct.\n\n4. Thousands: 9 (from first number) + 0 (second number) =9. Correct.\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 3 (first) +8 (second) =11. So write 1, carryover 1. Correct.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 9 (first) +2 (second) =11, plus 1 carried over is 12. So write 2, carryover 1. Correct.\n\n7. Millions place: 1 (first) +5 (second) =6, plus 1 carried over is 7. Correct.\n\n8. Ten millions place:7 (first) +0 (second) =7. Correct.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:1 +8 =9. Correct.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits we wrote are:.\n\nStarting from the ones: 6, then 0, 9,9,1 (from ten thousands place?), wait let me see:.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the sum step by step.\n\nAfter each step:.\n\nOnes: 6.\n\nTens: 0 (with carryover).\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:1 (and carryover 1).\n\nHundred thousands: 2 (carryover 1).\n\nMillions:7.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nWait, arranging the digits from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nThe digits would be:.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nSo the number is 9 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
