redo the addition step by step:.\n\nPositions (starting from 0):.\n\nPosition 0 (ones):.\n\n8 + 4 = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 1 (tens):.\n\n9 + 9 + 1 = 19 → 9, carry 1.\n\nPosition 2 (hundreds):.\n\n3 (from first number) + 8 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 3 (thousands):.\n\n1 (first) + 1 (second) + 1 (carryover) = 3 → 3, no carryover.\n\nPosition 4 (ten thousands):.\n\n3 (first) + 1 (second) = 4 → 4, no carryover.\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands):.\n\n9 (first) + 9 (second) = 18 → 8, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 6 (millions):.\n\n4 (first) + 0 (second) + 1 (carryover) = 5 → 5, no carryover.\n\nPosition 7 (ten millions):.\n\n7 (first) + 7 (second) = 14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 8 (hundred millions):.\n\n5 (first) + 8 (second) + 1 (carryover) = 14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the highest digit (hundred millions place) and there's still a carryover of 1, we need to add a new digit at the next higher place (billions place), which is 1.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left (positions 0 to 8 plus the new carryover):.\n\nThe digits from position 0 to 8 are:.\n\n2 (position0), 9 (pos1), 2 (pos2), 3 (pos3), 4 (pos4), 8 (pos5), 5 (pos6), 4 (pos7), 4 (pos8). .\n\nBut wait, the carryover after position8 was 1, so the final digit is 1 followed by the 4 from position8?.\n\nWait no, actually:.\n\nWait when you have position8 (hundred millions) gives 14, so you write down 4 and carryover 1. Since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place). So the digits from highest to lowest would be:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:4.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:4.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest (left to right):.\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 9 (tens)