 carry0.\n\nPosition7:\n\n0+7=7 +0=7. Sum7, carry0.\n\nPosition8:\n\n4+2=6 +0=6. Sum6, carry0.\n\nPosition9:\n\n6+8=14. Sum_digit=4, carry1.\n\nNow, after position9, there's a carryover of 1. Since there are no more digits, we add that as a new digit at the beginning (billions place).\n\nSo the total sum is 1 followed by the digits from position9 to 1:\n\nDigits are:\n\nBillions place:1,\n\nHundred millions:4,\n\nTen millions:6,\n\nMillions:7,\n\nHundred thousands:3,\n\nTen thousands:3,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:5,\n\nTens:4,\n\nOnes:2.\n\nPutting it all together, the number is 1,467,332,542.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method to ensure accuracy. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n640,127,023 + 827,205,519.\n\nLet me compute 640,127,023 + 800,000,000 = 1,440,127,023.\n\nThen add the remaining 27,205,519:\n\n1,440,127,023 +27,205,519 = ?\n\nAdding 27 million to 1,440,127,023 gives 1,467,127,023.\n\nThen add 205,519:\n\n1,467,127,023 + 205,519 = 1,467,332,542.\n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer is 1,467,332,542. I think that's correct.\n"]
