messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 405781934 and 259354502?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, so I need to add 405,781,934 and 259,354,502. Hmm, let me start by writing them down one on top of the other to align the digits properly. Let me see:.\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. The rightmost digits are the ones place. .\n\nStarting with the ones place: 4 (from the first number) and 2 (from the second number). Adding those gives 6. So the ones digit of the sum is 6.\n\nNext, the tens place: 3 and 0. That's 3. So the tens digit is 3.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 9 and 5. 9 + 5 is 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNow the thousands place: 1 (from the first number) plus 4 (from the second) plus the carried-over 1. That totals 6. So thousands digit is 6, no carryover here.\n\nTen-thousands place: 8 and 5. 8+5=13. Write 3, carry over 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 7 (from first number) and 3 (second number) plus the carried 1. 7+3=10 +1=11. So write 1 and carry over 1 again.\n\nMillions place: 0 (from first number) and 9 (second) plus the carried 1. 9 +1=10. So write 0 and carry over 1.\n\nTen-millions place: 4 (first number) and 5 (second) plus the carried 1. 4+5=9 +1=10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nHundred-millions place: The first number has 0 here, the second has 2, plus the carried 1. 2+1=3. So that's 3.\n\nWait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me go step by step again.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit from right to left:.\n\nPositions (starting from the right, position 1 is ones):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 4 + 2 = 6 ✔️.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 3 + 0 = 3 ✔️.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 9 +5=14 → 4 with carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 1 +4 +1 (carry) =6 ✔️.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 8 +5 =13 → 3, carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):7 +3 +1 (carry)= 11 → 1, carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):0 +9 +1 (carry)=10 → 0, carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):4 +5 +1 (carry)=10 →0, carryover1 ✔️.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):0 +2 +1 (carry)=3 ✔️. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
