inal answer is 815,529,349.\n\nWait, but in the initial digit-by-digit addition, I had the same result, so that's good. Maybe I should also check with another method. Let me try adding them step by step again.\n\nAlternatively, using column addition:\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned:\n\n       530,658,687\n     + 284,870,662\n     ----------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:7+2=9.\n\nTens:8+6=14 (4, carryover1).\n\nHundreds:6+6=12 plus carryover1 is 13 (3, carryover1).\n\nThousands:8+0=8 plus 1 is 9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:5 +7=12 (2, carryover1).\n\nHundred thousands:6 +8=14 plus 1 is 15 (5, carryover1).\n\nMillions:0 +4=4 plus 1=5, no carryover.\n\nTen millions:3 +8=11 (1, carryover1).\n\nHundred millions:5 +2=7 plus carryover1=8.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\n8 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions),5 (millions),5 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),3 (hundreds),4 (tens),9 (ones). So yes, 815,529,349. Okay, that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 815,529,349.\n"]
