final_output:  ['', "1,330,362,792?\n\nWait, let me verify this calculation another way.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:.\n\n940,174,722 + 390,188,070.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 940,174,722.\n\nAdd 390,188,070:\n\nAdding the millions first: 940 million + 390 million = 1,330 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 174,722 + 188,070.\n\n174,722 + 188,070 = let's see:\n\n174,722 + 188,070:\n\nAdding hundreds: 174,000 + 188,000 = 362,000.\n\nThen 722 + 70 = 792.\n\nSo total is 362,792.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 1,330,000,000 + 362,792 = 1,330,362,792.\n\nYes, that matches the earlier result. So the final answer should be 1,330,362,792.\n\nWait, but let me check the digits again with the previous step-by-step addition:\n\nThe positions from highest to lowest (billions down to ones):\n\nBillions: 1.\n\nHundred millions:3 (from 9+3 +1 carryover? Wait, the hundred millions place was 9 +3 =12 plus carryover 1? Wait in the previous step-by-step, when adding position9 (hundred millions), it was 9+3=12 plus the carryover from position8 (ten millions) which was 1, so total 13. Hence, the hundred millions digit is 3 with a carryover to billions.\n\nThus the billions digit is 1, then hundred millions is 3, ten millions is 3 (from position8: 4+9=13, so 3 with carryover1), etc.\n\nYes, so the total is indeed 1,330,362,792.\n\nTherefore, the answer is correct.\n"]
