g 269,873,892 + 546,861,563.\n\nLet me try adding them in parts.\n\n269,873,892 + 500,000,000 = 769,873,892\n\nThen add 46,861,563:\n\n769,873,892 + 46,861,563.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n769,873,892 + 40,000,000 = 809,873,892\n\nAdd 6,861,563:\n\n809,873,892 + 6,861,563.\n\nAdding 6,000,000 → 815,873,892\n\nThen add 861,563:\n\n815,873,892 + 800,000 = 816,673,892\n\nThen add 61,563 → 816,673,892 +61,563 = 816,735,455.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the sum is 816,735,455. Therefore, the final answer should be 816,735,455. I must have made a mistake in my first calculation when I thought the thousands place was 7+1, but actually, the thousands digit in the first number is 3, not 7. That was the key error. So the correct answer is 816,735,455.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 269,873,892 and 546,861,563 is \\boxed{816735455}.\n']
