rryover1,\n\n7+2=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1,\n\n3+6=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1,\n\n2+9=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1,\n\n3+3=6 +1=7 → so the digits would be:\n\nWait, let's do it properly:\n\nFirst number (32,374,341):\n\nDigit places (from right):\n\n1 (ones),\n\n4 (tens),\n\n3 (hundreds),\n\n4 (thousands),\n\n7 (ten thousands),\n\n3 (hundred thousands),\n\n2 (millions),\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n? Wait, actually 32,374,341 is 32 million, 374 thousand, 341.\n\nSo digits:\n\nPosition1:1,\n\nPosition2:4,\n\nPosition3:3,\n\nPosition4:4,\n\nPosition5:7,\n\nPosition6:3,\n\nPosition7:2,\n\nPosition8:3 (ten millions place? Wait no, 32 million is 3.2 crore, but in terms of digits:\n\nActually 32,374,341 is 3 (crore?), but in standard terms:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n32,374,341 is:\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n2 (millions),\n\n3 (hundred thousands),\n\n7 (ten thousands),\n\n4 (thousands),\n\n3 (hundreds),\n\n4 (tens),\n\n1 (ones).\n\nWait, perhaps I'm overcomplicating. Let me just do the addition:\n\n32,374,341\n\n+93,628,450\n\n=?\n\nAdding:\n\n32,374,341\n\n+93,628,450\n\n-------------\n\nStart from the right:\n\n1 +0 =1,\n\n4 +5 =9,\n\n3 +4 =7,\n\n4 +8 =12 (write 2, carryover1),\n\n7 +2 =9 +1 =10 (write 0, carryover1),\n\n3 +6 =9 +1 =10 (write 0, carryover1),\n\n2 +3 =5 +1 =6 (wait, the next digits are 2 (millions place of first number) and 9 (ten millions place of second number?) Wait, let me write them aligned:\n\n       32,374,341\n\n     +93,628,450\n\n     ------------\n\nAligning:\n\n      32,374,341\n\n    +93,628,450\n\n    =============\n\nLet's write them as:\n\n      32,374,341\n\n    +93,628,450\n\n    -------------\n\nAdding the ten millions place:\n\nFirst number has 3 (ten millions) and second has 9 (ten millions?), wait:\n\nWait, 32,374,341 is:\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n2 (millions),\n\n3 (hundred thousands),\n\n7 (ten thousands),\n\n4 (thousands),\n\n3 (hundreds),\n\n4 (tens),\n\n1 (ones).\n\nSecond number 93,628,450 is:\n\n9 (ten millions),\n\n3 (millions),\n\n6 (hundred thousands