ns:\n\n0 +80 =80.\n\nOnes:\n\n8 +7 =15.\n\nNow, summing all these components:\n\nStart with billions:\n\n1,100,000,000\n\nAdd hundred millions:\n\n1,100,000,000 +80,000,000 =1,180,000,000.\n\nAdd millions:\n\n1,180,000,000 +6,000,000 =1,186,000,000.\n\nAdd hundred thousands:\n\n1,186,000,000 +400,000 =1,186,400,000.\n\nAdd ten thousands:\n\n1,186,400,000 +31,000 =1,186,431,000.\n\nAdd thousands:\n\n1,186,431,000 +6,000 =1,186,437,000.\n\nAdd hundreds:\n\n1,186,437,000 +1,400 =1,186,438,400.\n\nAdd tens:\n\n1,186,438,400 +80 =1,186,438,480.\n\nAdd ones:\n\n1,186,438,480 +15 =1,186,438,495.\n\nWait, but this contradicts the previous result of 1,186,447,495. There's a discrepancy here. Which is correct?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an error in the first method. Let me check the first method again where I added vertically.\n\nFirst number: 970,333,908.\n\nSecond number:216,113,587.\n\nAdding vertically:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n          9 7 0 3 3 3 9 0 8\n        + 2 1 6 1 1 3 5 8 7\n        ---------------------\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nOnes:8+7=15 →5, carryover 1.\n\nTens:0+8=8 +1=9 →9, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds:9+5=14 →4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:3+3=6 +1=7 →7, carryover0.\n\nTen thousands:3+1=4 →4.\n\nHundred thousands:3+1=4 →4.\n\nMillions:0+6=6 →6.\n\nTen millions:7+1=8 →8.\n\nHundred millions:9+2=11 →1 (hundred millions place) and carryover 1 to billions.\n\nBillions:0+0 +1 (carryover) =1 →1.\n\nSo the digits from left to right (billions to ones):\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nHundred thousands:4,\n\nTen thousands:4,\n\nThousands:7,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nTens:9,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nThus the number is 1,186,447,495.\n\nBut in the component method, I get 1,186,438,495. There's a difference of 9,000. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's recheck the thousands place in the vertical addition.\n\nWait in the vertical addition, the thousands column is the 6th digit from the right (since positions are: ones (1)