 (hundred thousands):4.\n\nPosition7 (millions):3.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):4.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9.\n\nWait, perhaps this way is better. Let me reverse both numbers so that the rightmost digit is first, then we can add digit by digit.\n\nFirst number reversed: 2 6 3 4 0 3 7 5 3.\n\nSecond number reversed:4 2 2 7 3 4 3 4 9.\n\nNow adding each position from left to right (since reversed):.\n\nPosition1 (original ones place):.\n\n2 +4 =6. Write 6. No carry.\n\nPosition2 (original tens):.\n\n6 +2 =8. Write8. No carry.\n\nPosition3 (original hundreds):.\n\n3 +2=5. Write5. No carry.\n\nPosition4 (original thousands):.\n\n4 +7=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (original ten thousands):.\n\n0 +3 +1(carry)=4. Write4, no carry.\n\nPosition6 (original hundred thousands):.\n\n3 +4=7. Write7. No carry.\n\nPosition7 (original millions):.\n\n7 +3=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (original ten millions):.\n\n5 +4 +1(carry)=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (original hundred millions):.\n\n3 +9 +1(carry)=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the end, the carryover1 becomes a new digit at the next position. So the total reversed digits are:.\n\n1 (carry) followed by 3,0,0,4,7,4,5,1,6? Wait let me recount the reversed sum digits:.\n\nWait the reversed sum digits after each step:.\n\nAfter Position1:6.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:5.\n\nPosition4:1 (with carryover1).\n\nWait no, let me track the digits step by step:.\n\nLet me track each position's result and carry:.\n\nStart with carry=0.\n\nPosition1: 2+4=6 +0=6 → digit6, carry0.\n\nPosition2:6+2=8 +0=8 → digit8, carry0.\n\nPosition3:3+2=5 +0=5 → digit5, carry0.\n\nPosition4:4+7=11 → digit1, carry1.\n\nPosition5:0+3 +1=4 → digit4, carry0.\n\nPosition6:3+4=7 +0=7 → digit7, carry0.\n\nPosition7:7+3=10 → digit0, carry1.\n\nPosition8:5+4 +1=10 → digit0, carry1.\n\nPosition9:3+9 +1=13 → digit3, carry1.\n\nAfter all positions, the remaining carry is1, so we add that as the next digit.\n\nSo the reve