it, maybe I miscounted the places earlier. Let me recount the digits properly.\n\nWait, maybe I should write out the numbers with commas to clarify:.\n\n547,410,910.\n712,680,990.\n\nBreaking them down digit by digit from right to left (since commas are every three digits):.\n\nStarting from the right:.\nOnes: 0 and 0 → 0.\nTens: 1 and 9 → 10 (carry 1).\nHundreds: 9 and 9 → 18 +1=19 → 9, carry 1.\nThousands: 0 and 0 → 0 +1=1 (carry 0).\nTen thousands: 1 and 8 → 9, no carry.\nHundred thousands: 4 and 6 → 10 → 0, carry 1.\nMillions: 7 and 2 → 9 +1=10 → 0, carry 1.\nTen millions: 4 and 1 → 5 +1=6? Wait, hold on. Wait, the first number is 547,410,910. Let's parse each digit:.\n\nLet me list each digit position:.\n\nNumber1: 547,410,910.\nBreaking into digits (from right):.\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\n2 (tens):1.\n3 (hundreds):9.\n4 (thousands):0.\n5 (ten thousands):1.\n6 (hundred thousands):4.\n7 (millions):7.\n8 (ten millions):4.\n9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nNumber2: 712,680,990.\nDigits:.\nPosition1:0.\n2:9.\n3:9.\n4:0.\n5:8.\n6:6.\n7:2.\n8:1.\n9:7.\n\nSo adding each column:.\n\nPosition1: 0+0=0.\nPosition2:1+9=10 → 0, carry 1.\nPosition3:9+9 +1=19 → 9, carry1.\nPosition4:0+0 +1=1 → 1, no carry.\nPosition5:1+8=9 →9.\nPosition6:4+6=10 →0, carry1.\nPosition7:7+2 +1=10 →0, carry1.\nPosition8:4+1=5 +1 (carry) =6 →6.\nPosition9:5+7=12 → 2 and carry1? Wait, but there are no more digits beyond the hundred millions place. Wait, the first number has 9 digits (547,410,910) and the second also has 9 (712,680,990). Wait, actually, when adding, the highest place is the hundred millions (position9). But 5+7 in the hundred millions place would be 12. So that would be 2 in that place and carry over 1 to a new tenth position (billions place). .\n\nAh! I missed that earlier. So when adding the hundred millions (position9), 5 +7 =12. So we have to write 2 and carry over 1 to the next (billions) place. Since both numbers don't have a digit beyond that, the carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. .\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nPositions 1-9:.\n\nPosition1:0.\nPosition2:0 (carry1).\nPosition3:9 (carry1).\nPosition4:1.\nPosition5:9.\nPosition6:0 (carry1).\nPosition7:0 (carry1).\nPosition8:6.\nPosition9:2 (carry1).\nThen the carried 1 becomes the next digit (billions place: 1).\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 (billion) 2 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, let me reconstruct the number step by step.\n\nWait, let me write the digits from right to left as per each position:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\n\nPosition2 (tens):0 (with a carryover).\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):9.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0 (with carryover).\n\nPosition7 (millions):0 (with carryover).\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):6.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):2 (with carryover 1).\n\nThen the carryover 1 from position9 becomes the billions place.\n\nSo the digits from left to right (billions, hundred millions, .., ones):.\n\n1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
