billions place.\n\nSo the total is 1,2 (hundred millions) 6 (ten millions) 0 (millions) 0 (hundred thousands) 9 (ten thousands) 1 (thousands) 9 (hundreds) 0 (tens) 0 (ones). So combining these:\n\n1,260,091,900?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Let me add them numerically:\n\n547,410,910\n\n+712,680,990\n\nAdd the millions:\n\n547,410,910 is 547 million plus 410 thousand 910.\n\n712,680,990 is 712 million plus 680 thousand 990.\n\nAdding the millions: 547 +712 = 1,259 million.\n\nAdding the thousands parts: 410,910 + 680,990 = (410+680)*1000 + (910+990).\n\n410+680 =1,090 → 1,090,000.\n\n910+990=1,900.\n\nSo total thousands part is 1,090,000 +1,900 = 1,091,900.\n\nSo total sum: 1,259,000,000 +1,091,900 = 1,260,091,900.\n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer should be 1,260,091,900.\n\nWait, but in the digit-by-digit addition earlier, when adding the hundred millions place (5+7=12), so that gives 2 in that place and carryover1 to billions. So the billions place is 1, so total is 1,260,091,900. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 1,260,091,900.\n\nBut let me check with another approach, maybe using calculator-like steps:\n\n547,410,910\n\n+712,680,990\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +0 =0\n\n1+9 =10 → write 0, carry 1\n\n9 +9 +1 =19 → 9, carry1\n\n0 +0 +1 =1\n\n1 +8 =9\n\n4 +6 =10 →0, carry1\n\n7 +2 +1 =10 →0, carry1\n\n4 +1 +1 =6\n\n5 +7 =12 →2, carry1\n\nThen the final carryover 1 becomes the next digit.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n0,0,9,1,9,0,0,6,2 and then 1 in the next place.\n\nSo arranging from left to right (billions, hundred millions, etc.): 1 2 6 0 0 9 1 9 0 0 → which is 1,260,091,900. Yep, that's correct.\n\nSo the answer is correct. I think that's thorough.\n"]
