osition8: 9 (first) +7 (second) =16, plus the carried 1 is 17. So digit 7, carryover 1.\n\nPosition9:2 (first) +7 (second)=9, plus carried 1 =10. So digit 0, carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits from position 1 to 9 are:.\n\n3 (position1),6,8,7,7,3,5,7,0. Then the final carryover 1.\n\nSo the total sum is 1 followed by those digits. So the number is:.\n\n1 0 7 5 3 7 8 6 3?.\n\nWait, maybe I need to write it in order. Let's see:.\n\nThe digits, starting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition1:3.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:8.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:7.\n\nPosition6:3.\n\nPosition7:5.\n\nPosition8:7.\n\nPosition9:0.\n\nPlus the final carryover 1 as the next digit (the billions place). So putting them in order from left to right (highest to lowest place):.\n\nThe carryover 1 is the first digit (billions place?), then Position9's digit (0), then Position8's digit (7), Position7 (5), Position6 (3), Position5 (7), Position4 (7), Position3 (8), Position2 (6), Position1 (3). Wait, that would be:.\n\n1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (ones). Wait, that can't be right because the original numbers were 9-digit, so adding them would give a 10-digit number.\n\nWait, let me structure it properly.\n\nLet me write the sum step by step:.\n\nStart with the two numbers:.\n\n299,615,329.\n\n+775,762,534.\n\nLet me write them aligned:.\n\n          2 9 9 6 1 5 3 2 9.\n\n        + 7 7 5 7 6 2 5 3 4.\n\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n9 +4 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 2+3=5 +1=6. Write 6, no carry.\n\nHundreds:3+5=8. Write 8.\n\nThousands:5 +2=7. Write 7.\n\nTen thousands:1 +6=7. Write7.\n\nHundred thousands:6+7=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nMillions:9+5=14 +1=15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:9+7=16 +1=17. Write7, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:2+7=9 +1=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 