nPosition4 (ten thousands):2+0=2? Wait wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the digit positions here. Let me parse each number digit by digit properly.\n\nWait, perhaps I should write each number's digits in order. Let's take the first number: 748,521,299. Breaking down each digit from right to left:.\n\nDigits of 748521299:.\nPosition 0 (ones):9.\nPosition1:9.\nPosition2:2.\nPosition3:1.\nPosition4:2 (the fifth digit from the right).\nWait, maybe I'm getting confused here. Let's count properly:.\n\nThe number is 748,521,299. Let's remove commas: 7 4 8 5 2 1 2 9 9. Wait, that's 9 digits. Let's count positions from right (units) as position 0:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\nPosition0:9 (units).\nPosition1:9 (tens).\nPosition2:2 (hundreds).\nPosition3:1 (thousands).\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands).\nPosition5:5 (hundred thousands).\nPosition6:8 (millions).\nPosition7:4 (ten millions).\nPosition8:7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 937,024,529 → 9 digits as well:.\nDigits: 9 3 7 0 2 4 5 2 9.\n\nBreaking down:.\nPosition0:9 (units).\nPosition1:2 (tens).\nPosition2:5 (hundreds).\nPosition3:4 (thousands).\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands).\nPosition5:0 (hundred thousands).\nPosition6:7 (millions).\nPosition7:3 (ten millions).\nPosition8:9 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nStarting with Position0 (units):.\n9 +9 =18 → 8, carryover 1.\n\nPosition1 (tens):.\n9 (from first number) +2 (second number) =11, plus carryover 1 →12 →2, carryover1.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):.\n2 (first) +5 (second)=7 +1 →8, carryover0.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):.\n1 (first) +4 (second)=5 →5, carryover0.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):.\n2 (first) +2 (second)=4 →4, carryover0.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):.\n5 (first) +0 (second)=5 →5, carryover0.\n\nPosition6 (millions):.\n8 (first) +7 (second)=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):.\n4 (first) +3 (second)=7 +1 (carryover) →8, carryover0.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):.\n7 (first) +9 (second)=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we'v