repancy here. So where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, in the first method, when adding digit by digit, the result was 820,026,819, but in the second method, splitting the numbers, I get 821,026,819. There's a difference of 1,000,000. So I must have made an error in one of the steps.\n\nLet me check the digit-by-digit addition again.\n\nLet me write both numbers with all digits:\n\nFirst number: 5 0 5 8 4 0 9 4 8\n\nSecond number:3 1 5 1 8 5 8 7 1\n\nAdding each column from right (ones):\n\n1. Ones: 8 +1 =9. Correct.\n\n2. Tens:4 +7=11 \u2192 1, carryover1. Correct.\n\n3. Hundreds:9+8=17 +1=18 \u21928, carryover1. Correct.\n\n4. Thousands:0 +5=5 +1=6 \u21926. So thousands digit is 6. Correct.\n\n5. Ten thousands:4 (from first number) +8 (from second?) Wait, let's check the ten thousands place:\n\nFirst number: the digits are 5 (hundred millions),0 (ten millions),5 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),9 (hundreds),4 (tens),8 (ones).\n\nSecond number:3 (hundred millions),1 (ten millions),5 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),8 (hundreds),7 (tens),1 (ones).\n\nWait, in the ten thousands place:\n\nFirst number's ten thousands digit is 4.\n\nSecond number's ten thousands digit is 8.\n\nSo 4 +8 =12. So that's 2 with carryover1. Correct.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: first number's hundred thousands digit is 8, second's is1 (from the second number's hundred thousands place). So 8 +1 =9 + carryover1 \u219210. So 0 with carryover1. Correct.\n\n7. Millions place: first number has 5 (millions digit), second has5 (millions digit). 5+5=10 +1 (carryover)=11 \u21921 with carryover1. Correct.\n\n8. Ten millions place: first number has 0, second has1. 0+1=1 + carryover1 \u21922. Correct.\n\n9. Hundred millions:5 +3=8. Correct.\n\nSo the digits are indeed:\n\nHundred millions:8\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:9\n\nSo that's 8 2 1 0 2 6 8 1 9 \u21