arried 1 is 12. Write 2, carry over 1.\n\nFourth digit (thousands place):.\n4 + 9 = 13, plus the carried 1 is 14. Write 4, carry over 1.\n\nFifth digit (ten thousands place):.\n7 + 6 = 13, plus 1 is 14. Write 4, carry over 1.\n\nSixth digit (hundred thousands place):.\n0 + 8 = 8, plus 1 is 9. No carryover here.\n\nSeventh digit (millions place):.\n3 + 6 = 9. Still no carryover.\n\nEighth digit (ten millions place):.\n2 + 4 = 6.\n\nNinth digit (hundred millions place):.\n1 + 5 = 6.\n\nWait, let me check each step again carefully to avoid mistakes.\n\nStarting over step by step:.\n\nOnes place: 7 +6=13. Record 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 9 (from first number) + 0 (second number's tens place) =9 +1 (carryover) =10. So 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 3 +8=11 +1=12. So 2, carryover1.\n\nThousands place:4 +9=13 +1=14. So 4, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands place:7 +6=13 +1=14. So 4, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands place:0 +8=8 +1=9. So 9, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:3 +6=9. So 9.\n\nTen millions place:2 +4=6.\n\nHundred millions place:1 +5=6.\n\nPutting all together the digits from right to left (since we built it that way):.\n\nThe carried-over digits would have been handled, so the final number should be:.\n\nStarting from the ones digit we had 3, then 0, 2,4,4,9,9,6,6. Wait, but let's see the order.\n\nWait, when writing the sum, the digits are arranged from right to left as we compute, but the final number is written left to right. Let me list each digit's result:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n1. Ones: 3.\n2. Tens: 0.\n3. Hundreds:2.\n4. Thousands:4.\n5. Ten thousands:4.\n6. Hundred thousands:9.\n7. Millions:9.\n8. Ten millions:6.\n9. Hundred millions:6.\n\nSo putting them in order from highest to lowest place (left to right):.\n\nHundred millions (6), ten millions (6), millions (9), hundred thousands (9), ten thousands (4), thousands (4), hundreds (2), tens (0), ones (3). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
