digits from right to left (positions 1 to 10):.\n\nPosition10 (billions):1.\n\nPosition9:2.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition7:1.\n\nPosition6:8.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition4:3.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition1:1.\n\nWait, but when writing the number normally, it would be from highest to lowest. So the final number is 1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, maybe I need to reconstruct the number step by step.\n\nWait, let me list the digits step by step as we go from right to left (units to billions):.\n\nAfter adding each position:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1 (ones): 1 (with carryover 1).\n\n2 (tens):6.\n\n3 (hundreds):7.\n\n4 (thousands):3 (carryover 1).\n\n5 (ten thousands):1.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):8 (since first number's hundred thousands is 1, second's is 7 → 8, no carryover here?).\n\nWait wait, let me recast each step properly:.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nLet me write the two numbers aligned properly:.\n\n        6 3 3 1 0 6 0 0 7.\n\n      + 6 0 8 7 0 7 7 5 4.\n\n      --------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 7 +4 =11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 0 +5 +1 =6 → write6, carryover0.\n\nHundreds:0 +7 =7 → write7, carryover0.\n\nThousands:6 +7 =13 → write3, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:0 +0 +1=1 → write1, carryover0.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +7=8 → write8, carryover0.\n\nMillions:3 +8=11 → write1, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:3 +0 +1=4 → write4, carryover0.\n\nHundred millions:6 +6=12 → write2, carryover1.\n\nBillions: the carryover1 → write1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (positions 1 to 10):.\n\n1 (billions place digit is 1), then the next digits are 2 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait no, let's list them properly:.\n\nThe result digits are:.\n\nBillions place: 1.\n\nHundred millions: 2.\n\nT