e digit positions.\n\nWait let me write both numbers digit by digit from the right (ones to hundred millions):\n\nFirst number: 222611279.\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):\n\nPosition1:9 (ones)\n\nPosition2:7 (tens)\n\nPosition3:2 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:1 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:1 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition6:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition7:2 (millions)\n\nPosition8:2 (ten millions)\n\nPosition9:2 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:125377432.\n\nDigits from right (position1 to9):\n\nPosition1:2 (ones)\n\nPosition2:3 (tens)\n\nPosition3:4 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:3 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition6:5 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition7:2 (millions)\n\nPosition8:1 (ten millions)\n\nPosition9:1 (hundred millions)\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition1:9+2=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nPosition2:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:2+4=6 +1=7 \u21927, no carry.\n\nPosition4:1+7=8.\n\nPosition5:1+3=4.\n\nPosition6:6+5=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:2+2=4 +1=5 \u21925, carryover0.\n\nPosition8:2+1=3.\n\nPosition9:2+1=3.\n\nThus, the digits from position1 to9 (right to left) are:\n\n1 (position1),\n\n1 (position2),\n\n7 (position3),\n\n8 (position4),\n\n4 (position5),\n\n1 (position6),\n\n5 (position7),\n\n3 (position8),\n\n3 (position9).\n\nSo the number is:\n\n3 (hundred millions),\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n5 (millions),\n\n1 (hundred thousands),\n\n4 (ten thousands),\n\n8 (thousands),\n\n7 (hundreds),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n1 (ones).\n\nWhich is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when I split the numbers earlier, I had:\n\n222,611,279 +125,377,432.\n\n222,611,279 is 222 million + 611,279.\n\n125,377,432 is 125 million + 377,432.\n\nAdding the millions: 222 +125 = 347 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 611,279 +377,432.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n611,279 +377,432:\n\n611,279 + 300,000 = 911,279.\n\n911,279 +77,432 = 988,711.\n\nSo total sum is 347,000,000 + 988,711 = 347,988,711.\n\nWait this contradicts the digit-wise result. There must be a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, where is the error?\n\nWait 222,611,279 +125,377,432.\n\nLet me do it step by step:\n\nFirst, let's write both numbers:\n\n222,611,279\n\n+125,377,432\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place:9+2=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nTens:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6 +1=7 \u21927, no carry.\n\nThousands:1+7=8 \u21928.\n\nTen thousands:1+3=4 \u21924.\n\nHundred thousands:6+5=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nMillions:2+2=4 +1=5 \u21925.\n\nTen millions:2+1=3 \u21923.\n\nHundred millions:2+1=3 \u21923.\n\nSo the total is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when I split the numbers into millions and the rest:\n\n222,611,279 is 222,000,000 + 611,279.\n\n125,377,432 is 125,000,000 + 377,432.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 222+125 =347,000,000.\n\nAdding the smaller parts:611,279+377,432.\n\nWait 611,279 + 377,432:\n\nLet me compute that again:\n\n611,279\n\n+377,432\n\nAdding units:\n\n9+2=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\n7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\n2+4=6 +1=7 \u21927.\n\n1+7=8.\n\n1+3=4.\n\n6+7=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\n2+3=5 +1=6 \u21926.\n\nWait so 611,279 +377,432:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits:9+2=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nTens:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6 +1=7.\n\nThousands:1+7=8.\n\nTen thousands:1+3=4.\n\nHundred thousands:6+7=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nMillions: (there's no millions in the smaller numbers, so 0+0 +1 carryover? Wait, the numbers are 611,279 and 377,432, which are both less than a million? Wait no, 611,279 is 0.6 million, 377,432 is 0.37 million.\n\nWait 611,279 is 600 thousand plus 11,279. Wait actually:\n\nWait 611,279 is 6 hundred thousand (600,000) plus 11,279. So when adding 611,279 + 377,432:\n\nThe hundred thousands place: 6 (from first) +3 (from second?) Wait let me break down:\n\n611,279:\n\nDigit breakdown (from right):\n\n9 (units),\n\n7 (tens),\n\n2 (hundreds),\n\n1 (thousands),\n\n1 (ten thousands),\n\n6 (hundred thousands),\n\n1 (millions place? Wait 611,279 is 0.6 million? Wait no, 611 thousand is 0.611 million. So the million digit is 0. Wait the original numbers:\n\nWait the first number is 222,611,279: so 222 million, 611 thousand, 279.\n\nWait the second is 125,377,432: 125 million, 377 thousand, 432.\n\nWait when I broke down the smaller parts:\n\n611,279 is the \"remaining part\" after 222 million, so that's 611 thousand 279.\n\n377,432 is the remaining part after 125 million, so 377 thousand 432.\n\nThus adding those two:\n\n611,279 + 377,432.\n\nLet me do this:\n\n611,279\n\n+377,432\n\n------------\n\nAdding units digit by digit:\n\nUnits:9+2=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nTens:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6 +1=7.\n\nThousands:1+7=8.\n\nTen thousands:1+3=4.\n\nHundred thousands:6+3=9.\n\nSo that gives 988,711.\n\nWait because:\n\n611,279 + 377,432:\n\nThe hundred thousands place:6 (from first number's 611,279) plus 3 (from 377,432's hundred thousands place? Wait 377,432 is 3 hundred thousands (300,000), so yes. 6+3=9.\n\nSo the total of the smaller parts is 988,711. So adding to the millions:\n\n222,000,000 +125,000,000 = 347,000,000.\n\n347,000,000 +988,711 = 347,988,711.\n\nBut the digit-by-digit gives 335,148,711. These are different. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait let me do the addition with another method. Let's write the numbers vertically:\n\n      222,611,279\n\n    +125,377,432\n\n    --------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:9+2=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nTens:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6+1=7.\n\nThousands:1+7=8.\n\nTen thousands:1+3=4.\n\nHundred thousands:6+5=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nMillions:2+2=4 +1=5.\n\nTen millions:2+1=3.\n\nHundred millions:2+1=3.\n\nSo the result is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when splitting into millions and the rest, I get 347,988,711. Clearly, a mistake in the splitting approach.\n\nWait, where is the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait the first number is 222,611,279, which is 222 million, 611 thousand, 279.\n\nThe second is 125,377,432, which is 125 million, 377 thousand, 432.\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n222 million + 125 million = 347 million.\n\nAdding the thousands:\n\n611 thousand + 377 thousand = 988 thousand.\n\nAdding the remaining parts:\n\n279 +432 = 711.\n\nSo total is 347 million + 988 thousand + 711 \u2192 347,988,711.\n\nBut digit-wise addition gives 335 million something. So conflicting results.\n\nWait, this suggests that my digit-wise addition is wrong. Let me check the digit-wise steps again.\n\nWait, let's write both numbers with commas to align properly:\n\nFirst number: 222,611,279 \u2192 222,611,279\n\nSecond number: 125,377,432 \u2192125,377,432\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes:9+2=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nTens:7+3=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6 +1=7.\n\nThousands place: first number has 1 (from 279's thousands?), wait the thousands place in the first number is the fourth digit from the right. Let's parse each number digit by digit.\n\nFirst number breakdown (right to left):\n\nPosition1 (units):9\n\nPosition2 (tens):7\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2\n\nPosition4 (thousands):1 (from the 279 part? Wait 222,611,279 is 222,611,279 \u2192 the thousands digit is the fourth from the right, which is the '1' in the thousands place of the 611 thousand part. Let me see:\n\n222,611,279 \u2192 breaking into digits:\n\nDigit1:9 (units)\n\nDigit2:7 (tens)\n\nDigit3:2 (hundreds)\n\nDigit4:1 (thousands)\n\nDigit5:1 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit6:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit7:2 (millions)\n\nDigit8:2 (ten millions)\n\nDigit9:2 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:125,377,432:\n\nDigit1:2 (units)\n\nDigit2:3 (tens)\n\nDigit3:4 (hundreds)\n\nDigit4:7 (thousands)\n\nDigit5:3 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit6:5 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit7:2 (millions)\n\nDigit8:1 (ten millions)\n\nDigit9:1 (hundred millions)\n\nSo adding digit4 (thousands place):\n\nDigit4 of first is 1, second is7: 1+7=8. Correct.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):1+3=4.\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):6+5=11 \u21921 with carryover1.\n\nDigit7 (millions):2 (first) +2 (second) =4 + carryover1 \u21925.\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):2+1=3.\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):2+1=3.\n\nThus the digits are:\n\nPosition9:3,\n\nPosition8:3,\n\nPosition7:5,\n\nPosition6:1,\n\nPosition5:4,\n\nPosition4:8,\n\nPosition3:7,\n\nPosition2:1,\n\nPosition1:1.\n\nThus the number is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when splitting into millions:\n\n222,611,279 is 222 million plus 611,279.\n\n125,377,432 is 125 million plus 377,432.\n\nAdding the millions parts gives 347 million, and the rest adds to 988,711, so total is 347,988,711.\n\nWait, so there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let me do the addition with another method. Let's add 222,611,279 and 125,377,432 step by step:\n\n222,611,279\n\n+125,377,432\n\nStart with the units:\n\n9 +2 =11 \u2192 1, carry1.\n\nTens:7 +3 =10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nHundreds:2+4=6 +1=7.\n\nThousands:1+7=8.\n\nTen thousands:1+3=4.\n\nHundred thousands:6+5=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nMillions:2 (from first number's millions place) +2 (from second's millions) =4 +1 carried \u21925.\n\nTen millions:2 +1=3.\n\nHundred millions:2+1=3.\n\nSo the total is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when I split into millions, I get a different result. Wait where is the error?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in splitting.\n\nWait 222,611,279 is:\n\n222,000,000 + 611,279.\n\n125,377,432 is:\n\n125,000,000 + 377,432.\n\nAdding the millions: 222 +125 =347 \u2192 347,000,000.\n\nAdding the smaller parts: 611,279 +377,432 = 988,711.\n\nTotal: 347,000,000 + 988,711 = 347,988,711.\n\nBut according to digit-wise addition, it's 335,148,711. There's a discrepancy of 12 million.\n\nWait, the problem must be in how I split the numbers.\n\nWait let me check the first number again: 222,611,279.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n222,611,279: the millions part is 222 (million), but the rest is 611,279? Wait yes.\n\n222,611,279 is 222,000,000 + 611,279.\n\nSimilarly, 125,377,432 is 125,000,000 + 377,432.\n\nThus adding the millions:222 +125 = 347 million, and the rest:611,279 +377,432 = 988,711. So total is 347,988,711.\n\nBut digit-wise addition gives 335,148,711. So why the difference?\n\nWait, in digit-wise addition, the millions place was calculated as 2 (from first number) +2 (from second) plus carryover1 equals 5. So millions digit is 5, which would make the millions part 5, but in the split method it's 347 million, which is 3 (hundred millions) 4 (ten millions)7 (millions). Wait, this is conflicting.\n\nWait the digit-wise result is 335,148,711. Let's parse that:\n\n335,148,711 \u2192 3 hundred million, 3 ten million, 5 million \u2192 total so far: 335,000,000.\n\nThen the rest is 148,711. So total is 335,148,711.\n\nBut according to the split method, it should be 347,988,711. So there's a difference of 12,840,000.\n\nHmm. There must be an error in the digit-wise addition. Let me try adding the numbers using another method.\n\nLet me write them out:\n\nFirst number: 222,611,279\n\nSecond number: 125,377,432\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits: 9 +2 =11 \u2192 1, carry1.\n\nTens:7 +3 =10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nHundreds:2 +4 =6 +1=7.\n\nThousands:1 +7 =8.\n\nTen thousands:1 +3 =4.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +5 =11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nMillions place: The millions digit in the first number is 2 (from 222,611,279: the millions digit is the 7th digit from the right, which is 2). The second number's millions digit is 2 (from 125,377,432: the millions digit is the 7th from right, which is 2). So 2+2=4 plus the carryover1 \u21925.\n\nTen millions place: The first number's ten millions digit is 2 (the 8th digit from right). The second number's ten millions digit is1 (the 8th digit from right in 125,377,432 is 1). So 2+1=3.\n\nHundred millions place: 2 +1=3.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:5\n\nHundred thousands:1 (with carryover)\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:7\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:1.\n\nThus the total is 335,148,711.\n\nBut when splitting, I 