2, plus the carryover 1 makes 13. So we write 3 here and carry over 1.\n\nBillions place: The first number has 0 (since it's 564 million.. wait, actually, let me check the original numbers again. Wait, 564,680,097 is 5 hundred 64 million.., so the next digit is the hundred millions place. Wait, maybe I miscounted the places. Let me verify the digit positions again.\n\nWait, let's count the digits properly. Let me write both numbers without commas:.\n\nFirst number: 564680097 (9 digits).\nSecond number: 752231581 (9 digits).\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1: 7 + 1 = 8 (ones).\nPosition 2: 9 + 8 = 17 → 7 with carry 1 (tens).\nPosition 3: 0 + 5 + 1 = 6 (hundreds).\nPosition 4: 0 + 1 = 1 (thousands).\nPosition 5: 8 + 3 = 11 → 1 with carry 1 (ten thousands).\nPosition 6: 6 + 2 + 1 = 9 (hundred thousands).\nPosition 7: 4 + 2 = 6 (millions).\nPosition 8: 6 + 5 = 11 → 1 with carry 1 (ten millions).\nPosition 9: 5 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 13 → 3 with carry 1 (hundred millions).\nBut since both numbers are 9 digits, adding them could result in a 10-digit number. So the final carryover 1 would be the next digit (billions place).\n\nWait, so putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1 (ones): 8.\n\n2 (tens): 7.\n\n3 (hundreds): 6.\n\n4 (thousands): 1.\n\n5 (ten thousands): 1.\n\n6 (hundred thousands): 9.\n\n7 (millions): 6.\n\n8 (ten millions): 1 (but wait, when we added position 8 (ten millions), it was 6 +5 =11, so we wrote 1 and carried 1. Then adding the carryover to the next digit (position 9):.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 5 +7 +1 (carry from position 8) = 13. So that gives 3 in hundred millions, carryover 1.\n\nThen the next digit (position 10, which is billions place) is the carryover 1.\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 (billion), 3 (hundred million), then the rest as computed.\n\nPutting all digits together:.\n\nStarting from the highest place:.\n\nBillions: 1.\n\nHundred millions: 3.\n\nTen millions: 1 (from position 8).\n\nMillions: 6 (position 7).\n\nHundred thousands: 9 (position6).\n\nTen thousands: 1 (position5).\n\nThousands:1 (position4).\n\nHundreds:6 (position3).\n\nTens:7 (position2).\n\nOnes:8 (position1).\n\nWait, let me list them in order from left (billions) to right (ones):.\n\n1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 8 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
