the digits from the right, the first digit is ones, then tens, etc. So the result digits are:\n\nOnes:7\n\nTens:0\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:9\n\nTen millions:4\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nSo the number is 9 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, that would be 949,406,207. Let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers:\n\n102,261,353 + 847,144,854.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 100,000,000 + 800,000,000 = 900,000,000.\n\nThen 2,261,353 + 47,144,854. Wait, no, maybe better to break down:\n\n102,261,353 is 100,000,000 + 2,261,353.\n\n847,144,854 is 800,000,000 + 47,144,854.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 100M + 800M = 900M.\n\nThen 2,261,353 +47,144,854:\n\n2,261,353 +47,144,854 = ?\n\n2,261,353 + 40,000,000 = 42,261,353\n\nThen add 7,144,854: 42,261,353 + 7,144,854.\n\n42,261,353 +7,000,000 =49,261,353\n\nThen +144,854: 49,261,353 +144,854 = 49,406,207.\n\nSo total is 900,000,000 +49,406,207 = 949,406,207. So that's correct.\n\nSo the answer is 949,406,207.\n"]
