position4),\n\nHundreds:8 (position3),\n\nTens:7 (position2),\n\nOnes:3 (position1).\n\nSimilarly, 928,666:\n\nHundred thousands:9,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:8,\n\nHundreds:6,\n\nTens:6,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nAdding them:\n\nOnes:3+6=9,\n\nTens:7+6=13 \u21923, carry1,\n\nHundreds:8+6 +1=15 \u21925, carry1,\n\nThousands:5+8 +1=14 \u21924, carry1,\n\nTen thousands:5+2 +1=8,\n\nHundred thousands:7+9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nWait, so the total of the lower part is 1,684,539? Wait:\n\nWait the hundred thousands place is 16, so 6 with carryover1, but since there's no higher digits, that carryover would add to the millions. Wait, but the original breakdown was adding the millions first (131 +603) =734 million, and then adding the remaining parts (755,873 +928,666). But when adding the lower parts, their sum is:\n\nThe hundred thousands digit is 16, so 6 with a carryover of 1 to the millions. So total of the lower parts is 1,684,539? Let me compute 755,873 +928,666:\n\n755,873\n\n+928,666\n\n= (700,000 + 55,873) + (900,000 +28,666)\n\n= (700k +900k) + (55,873 +28,666)\n\n= 1,600,000 + 84,539 = 1,684,539.\n\nYes. So total sum is 734 million +1,684,539 = 735,684,539?\n\nWait, 734,000,000 +1,684,539 = 735,684,539. But according to the digit-by-digit addition earlier, I had 735,864,539. There's a discrepancy here. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nFirst method (digit by digit):\n\nThe total digits gave us 735,864,539.\n\nSecond method (split into millions and lower parts):\n\nGot 735,684,539.\n\nSo which is correct? Let me do the addition again carefully.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n131,755,873\n\n+603,928,666\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with the units:\n\n3 +6=9\n\nTens:7+6=13 \u21923, carry1\n\nHundreds:8+6=14 +1=15 \u21925, carry1\n\nThousands:5+8=13 +1=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nTen thousands:5+2=7 +1=8 \u21928, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands:7+9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nMillions:1+3=4 +1 (carry)=5.\n\nTen millions:3 +0=3.\n\nHundred millions:1+6=7.\n\nSo