hich were 131 +603 =734 million, adding the carryover1 from the hundred thousands place would make it 735 million, then the lower part becomes 684,539 (since 6 in hundred thousands, 8 in ten thousands, etc). Wait, let me see:\n\nThe lower part's total is 1,684,539 (from the correct calculation):\n\nWait, let me recompute 755,873 +928,666:\n\n755,873\n\n+928,666\n\nAdding digit-wise:\n\nHundred thousands:7+9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:5+2 +1 (carry)=8.\n\nThousands:5+8=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nHundreds:8+6=14 \u21924, carry1.\n\nTens:7+6=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nOnes:3+6=9.\n\nWait, no, the thousands place: 5 (from 755,873's thousands) and 8 (from 928,666's thousands). 5+8=13, plus the carryover from hundreds (wait, actually the order is from right to left):\n\nWait let me do it step by step properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n1. Ones:3+6=9.\n\n2. Tens:7+6=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\n3. Hundreds:8+6=14 +1=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\n4. Thousands:5+8=13 +1=14 \u21924, carry1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:5+2 +1 (carry)=8 \u21928, no carry.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7+9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nNow, since there are no higher digits beyond hundred thousands in the lower part, the carryover1 from the hundred thousands place would add to the millions place. Wait, but in the original split, the millions were already added separately (131 +603). So when adding the lower parts (755,873 +928,666), the total is 1,684,539 (since the carryover1 from the hundred thousands would be part of the million's place). Wait, perhaps the confusion is arising from how the numbers are split. Let me do the entire addition again properly:\n\nTotal sum:\n\n131,755,873\n\n+603,928,666\n\n= (100,000,000 +30,000,000 +1,000,000 +\n\n700,000 +50,000 +5,000 +\n\n800 +70 +3) +\n\n(600,000,000 +3,000,000 +\n\n900,000 +20,000 +8,000 +\n\n600 +60 +6).\n\nAdding all terms:\n\nHundred millions:100M +600M =700M.\n\nTen millions:30M +0 (since second number has 0 in ten millions) =30M.\n\nMillions:1M +3M