yover 1) followed by the digits from position9 to position1:\n\nSo the digits in order:\n\n1 (carryover), then position9 digit (3), position8 (3), position7 (5), position6 (2), position5 (1), position4 (0), position3 (5), position2 (8), position1 (2).\n\nWait that would be:\n\n1 (billion's place), 3 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions),5 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),5 (hundreds),8 (tens),2 (ones). So the number is 1,335,210,582.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions place) was the original highest, but with carryover, so the total is 1 followed by the digits.\n\nWait, let me structure it properly:\n\nThe digits we have after each position:\n\nStarting from the right (ones) to the left (billions):\n\nPositions 1-9 plus the carryover:\n\nThe written digits (from right to left):\n\nPosition1:2\n\nPosition2:8\n\nPosition3:5\n\nPosition4:0\n\nPosition5:1\n\nPosition6:2\n\nPosition7:5\n\nPosition8:3\n\nPosition9:3\n\nThen the carryover1 is the next digit to the left (position10).\n\nSo when written as a number, from left to right (billions to ones):\n\nPosition10:1,\n\nPosition9:3,\n\nPosition8:3,\n\nPosition7:5,\n\nPosition6:2,\n\nPosition5:1,\n\nPosition4:0,\n\nPosition3:5,\n\nPosition2:8,\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nSo combining these digits: 1,3 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions),5 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),5 (hundreds),8 (tens),2 (ones).\n\nThus the number is 1,335,210,582.\n\nWait, let me verify using another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n777,475,107\n\n+557,735,475\n\nLet me add the millions:\n\n777,475,107 is 777 million plus 475,107.\n\n557,735,475 is 557 million plus 735,475.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 777 +557 = 1,334 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 475,107 +735,475.\n\n475,107 +735,475:\n\nAdding 475,000 +735,000 = 1,210,000.\n\nThen 107 +475 = 582.\n\nSo total of those two parts: 1,210,582.\n\nTherefore total sum is 1,334,000,000 +1,210,582 = 1,335,210,582. Which matches the previous result. Okay, that seems correct. So the answer is 1,335,210,582.\n\nWait, but let me check again with another approach: maybe adding digit by digit again.\n\nFirst number: 7 7 7 4 7 5 1 0 7\n\nSecond number:5 5 7 7 3 5 4 7 5\n\nWait, perhaps I need to align the digits properly. Let me write them vertically:\n\n          7 7 7 4 7 5 1 0 7\n\n        + 5 5 7 7 3 5 4 7 5\n\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n7+5=12, write 2, carry 1.\n\nNext (tens):\n\n0+7=7 +1=8. Carry 0.\n\nHundreds:\n\n1+4=5. Carry 0.\n\nThousands:\n\n5+5=10, write 0, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:\n\n7+3=10 +1=11, write1, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:\n\n4+7=11 +1=12, write2, carry1.\n\nMillions:\n\n7+7=14 +1=15, write5, carry1.\n\nTen millions:\n\n7+5=12 +1=13, write3, carry1.\n\nHundred millions:\n\n7+5=12 +1=13, write3, carry1.\n\nThen the final carry1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n2,8,5,0,1,2,5,3,3,1.\n\nReversing them gives 1 3 3 5 2 1 0 5 8 2 → which is 1,335,210,582. Yep, same as before. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,335,210,582.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 777475107 and 557735475 is \\boxed{1335210582}.\n"] 60%|#####9    | 298/500 [7:01:37<3:51:46, 68.84s/it]
