ning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the last carryover:.\n\nThe total digits would now be 10 because of the final carryover. Let me write the result step by step:.\n\nStarting from position 1: 2.\n\nPosition 2: 3.\n\nPosition 3:6.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:1 (from millions place addition).\n\nPosition8:4 (from ten millions with carryover).\n\nPosition9:3 (from hundred millions plus carryover, but with a carryover 1).\n\nThen the final carryover 1 is the new digit at position10.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to position10 are:.\n\nPosition10:1.\n\nPosition9:3.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition7:1.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nWait, but when written as a number, we need to arrange them from highest to lowest position. So the final number would be:.\n\nStarting from position10 (the carryover) followed by position9 down to position1:.\n\n1 (from the final carryover) then 3 (position9), 4 (position8), 1 (position7), 5 (position6), 2 (position5), 4 (position4), 6 (position3), 3 (position2), 2 (position1). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
