o in my first reasoning I must have mixed up the positions. That\'s a mistake. So let\'s correct that.\n\nContinuing step by step properly now.\n\nContinuing:.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\nFirst number:1, second:1 → 1+1=2. Write 2, no carry.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\nFirst number:5, second:9 →5+9=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\nFirst number:3, second:6 →3+6=9, plus the carryover1 makes 10. So write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number:9, second:1 →9+1=10, plus carryover1 makes 11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we have to add the final carryover1 as the next digit (billions place). So the total becomes:.\n\nStarting from the highest digit (billions place):1, followed by the 1 (from the hundred millions place\'s result?), wait let\'s see:.\n\nWait after processing all positions up to 9 (hundred millions):.\n\nThe results so far, from position1 to position9:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1:9.\n\n2:0 (with carryover1).\n\n3:4.\n\n4:5.\n\n5:9.\n\n6:2.\n\n7:4 (since 5+9=14, so digit 4 and carryover1).\n\nWait, let me retrace step by step:.\n\nWait let me redo all steps properly, carefully:.\n\nStarting over with the positions:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):.\n\n6 +3 =9. Write 9. Carryover 0.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\n9 (from first) +1 (second) =10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\n1 +2 (since first number\'s hundreds is 1, second\'s is2) plus carryover1 →1+2+1=4. Write4, carryover0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\n1 (first) +4 (second)=5. Write5, carryover0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n3 (first) +6 (second)=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n1 (first) +1 (second)=2. Write2, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n5 (first) +9 (second)=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n3 (first) +6 (second)=9 + carryover1 → 10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n9 (first) +1 (second)=10 + carryover1 →11. Write1, carryover1.\n\