lions place:** The digits here are 2 and 9. Adding them plus the carry: 2 + 9 + 1 = 12. So, write 2 and carry over 1. But since there are no more digits left, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting all together, starting from the right, the digits are 8, 0, 2, 8, 0, 1, 4, 3, 2 with the final carried-over 1 at the front. So that would be 1,2,3,4,1,0,2,8,0,8. Wait, maybe I messed up the order here. Let me recount the places properly.\n\nWait, actually, when adding, each step corresponds to a specific place. Let me list each step's result again properly:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n- Ones: 8.\n- Tens: 0 (carry 1).\n- Hundreds: 2 (carry 1).\n- Thousands: 8.\n- Ten-thousands: 0 (carry 1).\n- Hundred-thousands: 1 (carry 1).\n- Millions: 4.\n- Ten-millions: 3 (carry 1).\n- Hundred-millions: 2 (carry 1).\n- Then the carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo combining all digits from right to left:.\n\nBillions place: 1.\n\nThen hundred-millions: 2.\n\nTen-millions: 3.\n\nMillions: 4.\n\nHundred-thousands: 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0.\n\nThousands: 8.\n\nHundreds: 2.\n\nTens: 0.\n\nOnes: 8. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
