\nPosition 10 (billions):1 (from the carryover)\n\nSo the total number is 1 followed by 0 (hundred millions), then 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 4 (ones). So the number is 1,040,112,844.\n\nLet me verify with another method. Let's add the numbers using another approach. Maybe breaking them into smaller parts.\n\nFirst number: 852,057,117\n\nSecond number: 188,055,727\n\nAdding them:\n\n852,057,117 + 188,055,727\n\nLet me add the millions:\n\n852,057,117 is 852,057,117\n\n188,055,727 is 188,055,727\n\nAdding the millions parts:\n\n852,000,000 + 188,000,000 = 1,040,000,000\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n57,117 + 55,727 = ?\n\n57,117 +55,727:\n\n57,000 +55,000 = 112,000\n\n117 +727 = 844\n\nSo total for the remaining parts: 112,000 + 844 = 112,844\n\nAdding to the millions total: 1,040,000,000 + 112,844 = 1,040,112,844. That matches the previous result. So the answer should be correct.\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,040,112,844.\n\nWait, but in the first step-by-step addition, the carryover was correctly accounted for. So yes, the answer is correct.\n"] 68%|######8   | 341/500 [7:58:02<3:16:30, 74.15s/it]
