04.\n\nSo total for the smaller parts: 1,099,000 + 804 = 1,099,804.\n\nAdding that to the 1,068 million:\n\n1,068,000,000 + 1,099,804 = 1,069,099,804.\n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another way:.\n\nLet me use calculator-like step-by-step addition:\n\nFirst number:770,876,131\n\nSecond number:298,223,673\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n1 +3 =4 (ones).\n\n3 +7 =10 → 0 with carryover 1 (tens).\n\n1 (hundreds) +6 (hundreds) +1 (carry) =8 (hundreds).\n\n6 (thousands) +3 (thousands) =9 (thousands).\n\n7 (ten thousands) +2 (ten thousands)=9 (ten thousands).\n\n8 (hundred thousands) +2 (hundred thousands)=10 → 0 with carryover 1 (hundred thousands).\n\n0 (millions) +8 (millions) +1 (carry) =9 (millions).\n\n7 (ten millions) +9 (ten millions) =16 →6 with carryover1 (ten millions).\n\n7 (hundred millions) +2 (hundred millions) +1 (carry)=10 →0 with carryover1 (hundred millions).\n\nFinally, the carryover1 becomes the billions digit.\n\nSo combining all digits gives 1,069,099,804. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 1,069,099,804.\n"]
