wn:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 1.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 9.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 2.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8.\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 0.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 5.\n\nNow, adding each position step by step, starting from position 1:.\n\nPosition 1: 4 +1 =5. Write down 5.\n\nPosition 2: 3 +1=4. Write 4.\n\nPosition 3: 8 +9=17. Oh, here we have a carryover. So write down 7, carryover 1.\n\nWait, but I need to remember the carryover for the next positions.\n\nWait, let me start over more carefully, keeping track of any carryover.\n\nStarting with Position 1 (ones):.\n\n4 +1 =5. No carryover. Result so far: 5.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):.\n\n3 +1 =4. No carryover. Now the number is 45.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):.\n\n8 +9 =17. So write 7, carryover 1. Now the result is 745.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):.\n\n0 +6 =6, plus the carryover 1 makes 7. So next digit 7. Result now 7745.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):.\n\n9 +2 =11, plus 0 carryover (since previous was 1, but that was handled in the thousands place). Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, after Position 3 (hundreds place), the carryover is 1 to the thousands place.\n\nSo Position 4 (thousands):.\n\n0 (from first number) +6 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) =7. Correct.\n\nNow moving to Position 5 (ten thousands):.\n\nFirst number has 9, second has 2. 9+2=11. No carryover from the previous step. Wait, but the previous step (thousands) didn't have a carryover beyond the 1 already accounted for. So 9+2=11. That gives 1 in the current position and carryover 1 to the next.\n\nWait, so Position 5:.\n\n9 +2 =11. So write down 1 and carryover 1. So the result so far is 1 (ten thousands place), but we have to consider the carryover. So the digits now are:.\n\nAfter Position 5: the current digit is 1, and carryover 1. So the current total digits from right would be ..17745? Wait, maybe I need to track this step by step.\n\nWait, let me structure this better.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1: 4+1=5 (no carryover).\n2: 3+1=4 (no carryover).\n3:8+9=17 (write 7, carryover 1).\n4:0+6 +1(carryover) =7 (write 7, no carryover).\n5:9 +2 =11 (write 1, carryover 1).\n6:5 +8 +1(carryover)=14 (write 4, carryover 1).\nWait, let's check position 6:.\n\nPosition 6 is hundred thousands place.\n\nFirst number has 5, second has 8. 5+8=13. Then add the carryover 1 (from position5) gives 14. So write 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):.\n\nFirst number has 8, second has 0. 8+0=8, plus carryover 1 =9. So write 9, no carryover.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):.\n\nFirst number has 7, second has 8. 7+8=15. So write 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number has 1, second has 5. 1+5=6, plus carryover 1 gives 7.\n\nNow, let me list all the digits from the highest to the lowest position:.\n\nPosition 9: 7.\n\nPosition 8:5.\n\nPosition7:9.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nWait, arranging them in order from highest to lowest (left to right):.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nMillions:9.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nTens:4.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nPutting them all together: 7 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 759,417,745?.\n\nWait, let me check that again. Wait, the positions:.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):7.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):9.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7.\n\nPosition2 (tens):4.\n\nPosition1 (ones):5.\n\nSo combining these digits:.\n\n7 (hundred millions) 5 (ten millions) 9 (millions) 4 (hundred thousands) 1 (ten thousands) 7 (thousands) 7 (hundreds) 4 (tens) 5 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 