(hundreds):2\n\nDigit8 (tens):5\n\nDigit9 (ones):6\n\nNow, adding digit by digit starting from the ones (rightmost):\n\nDigit9 (ones place):0 +6=6. Write 6.\n\nDigit8 (tens):9 +5=14 → write 4, carryover1.\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):5 +2=7 +1=8 → write8, carryover0.\n\nDigit6 (thousands):9 +3=12 → write2, carryover1.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):0 +3=3 +1=4 → write4, carryover0.\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):7 +1=8 → write8, carryover0.\n\nDigit3 (millions):9 +6=15 → write5, carryover1.\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):3 +9=12 +1 (carryover)=13 → write3, carryover1.\n\nDigit1 (hundred millions):8 +3=11 +1 (carryover)=12 → write2, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the highest digit (hundred millions), we have a carryover of 1 which becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo putting it all together, from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place:1,\n\nHundred millions:2,\n\nTen millions:3,\n\nMillions:5,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:4,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:8,\n\nTens:4,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, let me list them in order:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:2,\n\nTen millions:3,\n\nMillions:5,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:4,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:8,\n\nTens:4,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, that seems inconsistent with previous steps. Let me list each digit's position again.\n\nWait, the digits after addition are:\n\nStarting from the highest (billions place):\n\nBillions:1 (carryover),\n\nHundred millions:2,\n\nTen millions:3,\n\nMillions:5,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:4,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:8,\n\nTens:4,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, but how does that translate into the number? Let's see:\n\nThe digits from left to right (highest to lowest) would be:\n\n1 (billions),\n\n2 (hundred millions),\n\n3 (ten millions),\n\n5 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands),\n\n4 (ten thousands),\n\n2 (thousands),\n\n8 (hundreds),\n\n4 (tens),\n\n6 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,235,842,846.\n\nWait, so that would be the correct sum.\n\nWait, but in my first calculation,