. Adding the carryover 1 gives 7. So millions digit is 7, no carryover this time.\n\nMoving to the ten millions place. The first number has a 9 and the second has a 7. 9 + 7 = 16. So we put 6 in the ten millions place and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred millions place. The first number has a 4 and the second has a 2. 4 + 2 = 6. Adding the carried over 1 gives 7. So the hundred millions digit is 7. .\n\nWait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Let me go through each digit again:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6 +1 =7 ✔️.\n\nTens:0+7=7 ✔️.\n\nHundreds:0+1=1 ✔️.\n\nThousands:8+7=15, so 5 with carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands:7+2 +1 (carry) =10 → 0 with carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands:8+2 +1 =11 →1 with carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nMillions:5+1 +1=7 ✔️.\n\nTen millions:9+7=16 →6 with carryover 1 ✔️.\n\nHundred millions:4+2 +1=7 ✔️.\n\nWait, but the first number is 495,878,006. So the digits from right to left are:.\n\n6 (ones),0 (tens),0 (hundreds),8 (thousands),7 (ten thousands),8 (hundred thousands),5 (millions),9 (ten millions),4 (hundred millions). Wait, actually, let me confirm the place values. .\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me write both numbers with commas to clarify:.\n\nFirst number: 495,878,006. Breaking it down:.\n\n- The digits are 4 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 271,227,171. Breaking it down:.\n\n- 2 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),1 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),1 (hundreds),7 (tens),1 (ones).\n\nWait, so when adding, the digits should be aligned properly:.\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically:.\n\n          4 9 5 8 7 8 0 0 6.\n        + 2 7 1 2 2 7 1 7 1.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n6 +1 =7 → ones place:7.\n\nTens: 0 +7 =7 → tens:7.\n\nHundreds:0 +1 =1 → hundreds:1.\n\nThousands:8 +7 =15 → write 5, carryover 1 → thousands:5, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (from first number) +2 (second) +1 (carry) =10 → write 0, carryover1 → ten thousands:0, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:8 (first) +2 (second) +1 (carry) =11 → write 1, carryover1 → hundred thousands:1, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 (first) +1 (second) +1 (carry) =7 → millions:7, no carryover.\n\nTen millions:9 (first) +7 (second) =16 → write 6, carryover1 → ten millions:6, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:4 +2 +1 (carryover) =7 → hundred millions:7. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
