ions:\n\n1 (ones):0\n\n2 (tens):3\n\n3 (hundreds):1\n\n4 (thousands):4\n\n5 (ten thousands):6\n\n6 (hundred thousands):3\n\n7 (millions):6\n\n8 (ten millions):5\n\n9 (hundred millions):7\n\nSo adding each column from right to left:\n\nColumn 1 (ones):7 + 0 =7.\n\nColumn 2 (tens):9 +3=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nColumn3 (hundreds):8 +1=9 plus carryover 1=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nColumn4 (thousands):2+4=6 plus 1=7. Write7, no carryover.\n\nColumn5 (ten thousands):3+6=9. Write9, no carryover.\n\nColumn6 (hundred thousands):7+3=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nColumn7 (millions):1+6=7 plus1=8. Write8, no carryover.\n\nColumn8 (ten millions):0+5=5. Write5, no carryover.\n\nColumn9 (hundred millions):7+7=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nNow, the carryover1 goes to the next column (billions place, which is the 10th digit). So the total is 1 followed by the digits we have: 1 4 5 8 0 9 7 0 2 7.\n\nWait, so the digits from billions down to ones would be:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:2\n\nOnes:7.\n\nSo the number is 1,458,097,027. Wait, but when I first thought I had 1,458,097,207, that was wrong because I miscalculated the hundreds place. So the correct total is 1,458,097,027. Let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers:\n\n701,732,897 +756,364,130.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n701,732,897 is 701 million plus 732,897.\n\n756,364,130 is 756 million plus 364,130.\n\nAdding the millions:701 +756 =1,457 million.\n\nNow the remaining parts:732,897 +364,130.\n\nAdding those:\n\n732,897 +364,130.\n\n732,897 +300,000 =1,032,897.\n\n1,032,897 +64,130 =1,097,027.\n\nSo total is 1,457,000,000 +1,097,027 =1,458,097,027. Yes, that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 1,458,097,027.\n\nI think initially I might have mixed up the hundreds and tens place in the intermediate steps, but upon breaking it down again and verifying 