r.\n\n8 +2=10, carryover1.\n\n7 +8 +1=16, carryover1.\n\n3 +1 +1=5.\n\nWait let me do step by step:\n\nUnits: 6+5=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTens:9+0=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:2+3=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nThousands:8+2=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7 +8=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:3+1=4 +1=5 →5, no carryover.\n\nSo the total of the lower part is 560,601.\n\nAdding to the 1,010,000,000 (from 879M +131M=1,010M):\n\nWait, actually the total would be 1,010,000,000 + 560,601 =1,010,560,601. Which matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the final sum is 1,010,560,601. Let me confirm once again with another method, perhaps using calculator approximation.\n\nBut since I can't use a calculator, maybe breaking into parts:\n\n879,378,296 +131,182,305.\n\nLet me add 879,378,296 + 100,000,000 = 979,378,296.\n\nThen add 31,182,305 to that: 979,378,296 +31,182,305.\n\nAdding 30,000,000: 979,378,296 +30,000,000 =1,009,378,296.\n\nThen add 1,182,305: 1,009,378,296 +1,182,305.\n\nAdding 1,000,000: 1,010,378,296.\n\nThen add 182,305: 1,010,378,296 +182,305 = 1,010,560,601. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,010,560,601. Let me just ensure that in the initial digit-by-digit addition I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait in the hundreds place, when adding 2 (from first number) +3 (second) +1 (carryover from tens) equals 6, correct.\n\nThousands place: 8 +2=10, so 0 with carryover, correct.\n\nTen thousands:7+8=15, plus carryover1 makes 16 →6, carryover1. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +1 +1=5. Correct.\n\nMillions:9+1=10 →0 and carryover1. Correct.\n\nTen millions:7 +3 +1 (carryover)=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:8+1 +1 (carryover)=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nBillions:1 from carryover. So the digits are 1 followed by 0,1,0,5,6,0,6,0,1 → yes, that's 1,010,560,601.\n\nAlright, looks consistent. So the answer is correct.\n"]
