over 1.\n\n7. Millions:3 +4 =7 +1=8. Write8, no carryover.\n\n8. Ten millions:6 +4 =10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\n9. Hundred millions:5 +7 =12 +1 (carryover)=13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit at the beginning (billions place): 1.\n\nPutting all together, the digits from right to left would be:.\n\nStarting from the ones: 8,8,6,6,3,0,8,0,3 and the carryover 1. Wait, let me structure it properly:.\n\nThe digits from right to left after each step are:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:8.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:3 (with a carryover).\n\nHundred thousands:0 (with carryover).\n\nMillions:8.\n\nTen millions:0 (with carryover).\n\nHundred millions:3 (with carryover).\n\nThen the carryover 1 as the next digit.\n\nSo arranging them from highest to lowest place:.\n\nThe final digits would be:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:3.\n\nTen millions:0.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nTens:8.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nWait, maybe I need to reconstruct the number step by step. Let's list the digits in order from the highest place (billions) down:.\n\nThe result has a billions digit of 1, then hundred millions 3, ten millions 0, millions 8, hundred thousands 0, ten thousands 3, thousands 6, hundreds 6, tens 8, ones 8.\n\nWait, but let me write it out properly:.\n\nStarting from the left (billions place):.\n\n1 (billions).\n\n3 (hundred millions).\n\n0 (ten millions).\n\n8 (millions).\n\n0 (hundred thousands).\n\n3 (ten thousands).\n\n6 (thousands).\n\n6 (hundreds).\n\n8 (tens).\n\n8 (ones).\n\nWait, but the ten millions place was the 8th digit from the right. Wait, perhaps I need to re-express this in terms of the digit positions.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's better to write the sum step by step:.\n\nLet me try adding the numbers vertically:.\n\n          5 6 3 0 6 2 4 3 8.\n        + 7 4 4 9 7 4 2 5 0.\n        -------------------