firm with another approach. Let's add the two numbers as:\n\n275,769,705 + 659,353,361.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n275,769,705 + 659,353,361 = (200,000,000 + 70,000,000 + 5,000,000 + 700,000 + 60,000 + 9,000 + 700 + 0 +5) + (600,000,000 + 50,000,000 +9,000,000 + 300,000 +50,000 +3,000 +300 +60 +1).\n\nAdding each component:\n\n200,000,000 +600,000,000 =800,000,000.\n\n70,000,000 +50,000,000 =120,000,000.\n\n5,000,000 +9,000,000 =14,000,000.\n\n700,000 +300,000 =1,000,000.\n\n60,000 +50,000 =110,000.\n\n9,000 +3,000 =12,000.\n\n700 +300 =1,000.\n\n0 +60 =60.\n\n5 +1=6.\n\nNow add all those:\n\n800,000,000\n\n+120,000,000 =920,000,000\n\n+14,000,000 =934,000,000\n\n+1,000,000 =935,000,000\n\n+110,000 =935,110,000\n\n+12,000 =935,122,000\n\n+1,000 =935,123,000\n\n+60 =935,123,060\n\n+6 =935,123,066.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the final answer should be 935,123,066.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another method. Let me add them digit by digit again:\n\n275,769,705\n\n+659,353,361\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n  2 7 5 7 6 9 7 0 5\n\n+6 5 9 3 5 3 3 6 1\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n5 +1 =6. Next digit (tens):\n\n0+6=6. Next (hundreds):\n\n7+3=10, write 0, carryover1.\n\nThousands:9+3=12 +1=13 → 3, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:6+5=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:7+3=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5+9=14 +1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:7+5=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:2+6=8 +1=9 →9.\n\nSo the total is 935,123,066. Looks correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 935,123,066.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 275769705 and 659353361 is \\boxed{935123066}.\n"]
