\n\nHundred thousands:7 (Wait, position5 is ten thousands. Let me re-express each position properly.\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to list each digit step by step.\n\nThe positions:.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\n1. Ones: 8+0=8.\n\n2. Tens:4+0=4.\n\n3. Hundreds:0+3=3.\n\n4. Thousands:2+7=9.\n\n5. Ten thousands:4+3=7.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:8+8=16 → 6 with carryover 1.\n\n7. Millions:7 +4 +1 (carryover) → 12 → 2, carryover 1.\n\n8. Ten millions:6 +2 +1 (carryover) →9, no carryover.\n\n9. Hundred millions:8 +6 =14 →4, carryover1.\n\n10. Billions: carryover1 (since there are no digits beyond hundred millions except the carryover).\n\nSo the digits from left (billions) to right (ones):.\n\nBillions digit:1.\n\nHundred millions:4.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nHundred thousands:7 (Wait, position6 is hundred thousands, which is 16, so the digit there is 6, but position5 is ten thousands which is 7. Let me list each digit in the correct order.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to write the digits in order from the highest place to the lowest.\n\nThe highest place here is billions, which is 1.\n\nThen hundred millions:4.\n\nThen ten millions:9.\n\nMillions place:2 (from position7, which is millions place, which was 7+4+1=12 → digit 2).\n\nHundred thousands place:6 (from position6, which is hundred thousands: 8+8=16, so digit 6).\n\nTen thousands place:7 (position5).\n\nThousands place:9 (position4).\n\nHundreds place:3 (position3).\n\nTens place:4 (position2).\n\nOnes place:8 (position1).\n\nSo putting all together:.\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),3 (hundreds),4 (tens),8 (ones). .\n\nWait, let me check the positions again carefully.\n\nWait, perhaps I should structure the numbers vertically:.\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned properly:.\n\n          8 6 7 8 4 2 0 4 8.\n        + 6 2 4 8 3 7 3 0 0.\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\