e?\n\nWait, perhaps in the breakdown, I added the millions parts wrong? Let me check the first number's breakdown.\n\nWait 226,798,201: the millions part is 226, so 226,000,000. The remainder is 798,201.\n\nSimilarly, second number:809,216,897 is 809,000,000 +216,897.\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nAdding those:\n\n226,000,000 +809,000,000 =1,035,000,000.\n\nAdding remainders:798,201+216,897=1,015,098.\n\nTotal:1,035,000,000 +1,015,098 =1,036,015,098.\n\nBut the digit-by-digit method says 1,030,150,908. So discrepancy of 5,864,190.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in digit-by-digit calculation.\n\nWait let me re-calculate digit-by-digit again step by step carefully.\n\nFirst number:226,798,201.\n\nDigits from right to left (positions 0 to 8):\n\nPosition0 (ones):1.\n\nPosition1 (tens):0.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):2.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):8.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):9.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):7.\n\nPosition6 (millions):6.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):2.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):2.\n\nSecond number:809,216,897.\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nPosition0:7.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:9.\n\nPosition7:0.\n\nPosition8:8.\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition0:1+7=8 → 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition1:0+9=9 →9, no carryover.\n\nPosition2:2+8=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:8+6=14 +1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:9+1=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:7+2=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition6:6+9=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:2+0=2 +1=3 →3, no carryover.\n\nPosition8:2+8=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nAfter all positions, the carryover1 from position8 (hundred millions) becomes a new digit at position9 (billions).\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nPosition9:1.\n\nPosition8:0.\n\nPosition7:3.\n\nPosition6:6.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition3:5.\n\nPosition2:0.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition0:8.\n\nSo the number is 1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),0 (hundreds),9 (tens),8 (ones).\n\nThat is: 1,030,150,908.\n\nBut according to the breakdown method, it's 1,036,015,098. So there is a discrepancy of 5,864,190.\n\nWait, let's compute the difference between the two results:\n\n1,036,015,098 (breakdown) minus 1,030,150,908 (digit-by-digit) =5,864,190.\n\nHmm. So which one is correct?\n\nLet me use another method: adding the two numbers directly in parts.\n\nLet me compute 226,798,201 +809,216,897.\n\nLet me add 226,798,201 +800,000,000 =1,026,798,201.\n\nThen add the remaining 9,216,897.\n\nWait 809,216,897 is 800,000,000 +9,216,897.\n\nSo adding to 226,798,201:\n\n226,798,201 +800,000,000 =1,026,798,201.\n\nNow add 9,216,897:\n\n1,026,798,201 +9,216,897.\n\nLet's compute this step by step:\n\n1,026,798,201\n\n+     9,216,897\n\n=?\n\nAdding the numbers:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes:1+7=8.\n\nTens:0+9=9.\n\nHundreds:2+8=10 →0 carryover1.\n\nThousands:8+6=14 +1=15 →5 carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9+1=10 +1=11 →1 carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:7+2=9 +1=10 →0 carryover1.\n\nMillions:6+9=15 +1=16 →6 carryover1.\n\nTen millions:2 (from first number's ten millions) +0 (from second's ten millions) +1 (carryover) =3.\n\nHundred millions:0 (since first number's hundred millions is 0 in the second part?) Wait no.\n\nWait let me do this properly:\n\nWait the first number after adding 800 million is 1,026,798,201. Let's break it down:\n\n1,026,798,201 is 1,000,000,000 +26,798,201.\n\nAdding 9,216,897 to that:\n\nTotal becomes 1,000,000,000 + (26,798,201 +9,216,897).\n\nCompute 26,798,201 +9,216,897:\n\n26,798,201 +9,216,897.\n\nAdding:\n\n26,798,201\n\n+9,216,897\n\n=?\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes:1+7=8.\n\nTens:0+9=9.\n\nHundreds:2+8=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nThousands:8+6=14 +1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9+1=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:7+2=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nMillions:6+9=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:2 (from 26 million's ten millions?