lator-like addition:\n\n599,051,963\n\n+738,423,059\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nStart with the millions:\n\n599,051,963 is 599,051,963.\n\n738,423,059 is 738,423,059.\n\nAdding:\n\n599,051,963\n\n+738,423,059\n\n= (500,000,000 + 99,051,963) + (700,000,000 +38,423,059)\n\n= (500M +700M) + (99,051,963 +38,423,059)\n\n=1,200,000,000 + (137,475,022) → Wait, 99,051,963 +38,423,059:\n\n99,051,963 +38,423,059:\n\nAdding:\n\n99,051,963\n\n+38,423,059\n\n= (99,000,000 +51,963) + (38,000,000 +423,059)\n\n= (99,000,000 +38,000,000) + (51,963 +423,059)\n\n=137,000,000 + (475,022) → total 137,475,022.\n\nThen total sum is 1,200,000,000 +137,475,022 =1,337,475,022. Yep, same as before.\n\nSo the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,337,475,022. But the problem might require it without commas, so 1337475022. Let me check the digit count.\n\nWait, the first number is 9 digits, second is 9 digits, so sum can be up to 10 digits. The result is 1,337,475,022 which is 10 digits. So yes.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 1337475022. But in the template, they want the Answer section to have <<answer>>, so I'll format it accordingly.\n"]
