      "text": "781,717,402?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the places. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I miscounted the digits. Let me write each digit position clearly.\n\nLet me list each number's digits from right to left (since we add from the right):\n\nFirst number: 550,935,639\nDigits (right to left): 9 (1s), 3 (10s), 6 (100s), 5 (1k), 3 (10k), 9 (100k), 0 (1M), 5 (10M), 5 (100M)\n\nSecond number: 230,781,763\nDigits (right to left): 3 (1s), 6 (10s), 7 (100s), 1 (1k), 8 (10k), 7 (100k), 0 (1M), 3 (10M), 2 (100M)\n\nNow, adding each column starting from the right (1s place):\n\n1. Ones place: 9 + 3 =12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n2. Tens: 3 +6 +1 =10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n3. Hundreds:6 +7 +1 =14 \u21924, carryover1\n4. Thousands:5 +1 +1=7 \u21927, no carryover\n5. Ten thousands:3 +8=11 \u21921, carryover1\n6. Hundred thousands:9 +7 +1=17 \u21927, carryover1\n7. Millions:0 +0 +1=1 \u21921, no carryover\n8. Ten millions:5 +3=8 \u21928\n9. Hundred millions:5 +2=7 \u21927\n\nPutting it all together from right to left, the digits would be 2,0,4,7,1,7,1,8,7. Wait, but that's reversed. Let me see:\n\nWait the digits from the addition steps are:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nFirst digit (ones):2\n\nSecond (tens):0\n\nThird (hundreds):4\n\nFourth (thousands):7\n\nFifth (ten thousands):1\n\nSixth (hundred thousands):7\n\nSeventh (millions):1\n\nEighth (ten millions):8\n\nNinth (hundred millions):7\n\nSo arranging them from highest to lowest place value (left to right), it's 7 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands?), wait, maybe I need to check the order again.\n\nWait, the positions are:\n\nThe first digit (rightmost) is ones (position 1), then tens (position2), up to the ninth digit (hundred millions place). So the final digits in order from left to right are:\n\nHundred millions place: 7\n\nTen millions place:8\n\nMillions place:1\n\nHundred thousands place:7\n\nTen thousands place:1\n\nThousands place:7