6 (second's thousands) =7. plus carry1 →8. digit8, carry0.\n\n5. pos5:.\n\n9 (ten thousands) +1 (ten thousands) =10 →0, carry1.\n\n6. pos6:.\n\n2 (hundred thousands) +6 (hundred thousands) =8 + carry1 →9. digit9, carry0.\n\n7. pos7 (millions):.\n\n6 +6 =12 → digit2, carry1.\n\n8. pos8 (ten millions):.\n\n3 (ten millions) +6 (ten millions) =9, plus carry1 →10 → digit0, carry1.\n\n9. pos9 (hundred millions):.\n\n9 +5 =14, plus carry1 →15 → digit5, carry1.\n\nThen pos10:1.\n\nWait, so the digits now are:.\n\npos1:0.\n\npos2:7.\n\npos3:0.\n\npos4:8.\n\npos5:0.\n\npos6:9.\n\npos7:2.\n\npos8:0.\n\npos9:5.\n\npos10:1 (from carry).\n\nWait let's list them from pos10 down:.\n\npos10:1.\n\npos9:5.\n\npos8:0.\n\npos7:2.\n\npos6:9.\n\npos5:0.\n\npos4:8.\n\npos3:0.\n\npos2:7.\n\npos1:0.\n\nSo arranging these digits from highest to lowest:.\n\n1 (billions),5 (hundred millions),0 (ten millions),2 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),0 (hundreds),7 (tens),0 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
