 =6 plus the carried 1 makes 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:1 +8 =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands:8 +8=16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:1 +0=1 plus the carried 1 =2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +1=5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nMillions:0 +5=5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nTen millions:4 +4=8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions:9 +2=11. Write 11. So putting it all together, the sum would be 1,185,526,973?\n\nWait, let me check again. Wait, maybe I made a mistake in the thousands place.\n\nWait let's do it step by step again carefully:\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically:\n\n       9 4 0 4 1 8 1 2 9\n     + 2 4 5 1 0 8 8 4 4\n     --------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\nOnes: 9 +4 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 2 +4 =6, plus the 1 carried over is 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:1 +8 =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:8 (from first number) +8 (from second number) =16. So write 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:1 (from first number's ten thousands) +0 (from second number's ten thousands) =1, plus the carried over 1 makes 2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:4 (from first number) +1 (from second number) =5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:0 (first) +5 (second) =5. Write 5.\n\nTen millions place:4 (first) +4 (second) =8. Write 8.\n\nHundred millions place:9 (first) +2 (second) =11. So here, we have to write 1 in the hundred millions place and carryover 1 to the next (billions) place. Since there are no higher digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting all the digits together with the carryover from the hundred millions:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:3\n\nTens:7\n\nHundreds:9\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nMillions:5\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:1 (from 9+2=11, but we have a carryover 1 to billions)\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nSo the total is 1,185,526,973. Let me confirm this with another method, maybe adding the numbers step by step in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 940,418,129 + 245,108,844:\n\nFirst, add 940,418,129 + 200,000,000 = 1,140,418,129\n\nThen add 45,108,844 (since 245 million minus 200 million is 45 million):\n\nWait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n245,108,844 can be split into 200,000,000 + 45,000,000 + 108,844.\n\nSo adding to 940,418,129:\n\nFirst add 200,000,000: 940,418,129 + 200,000,000 = 1,140,418,129\n\nThen add 45,000,000: 1,140,418,129 +45,000,000 = 1,185,418,129\n\nNow add the remaining 108,844: 1,185,418,129 + 108,844.\n\nLet's do that:\n\n1,185,418,129 + 100,000 = 1,185,518,129\n\nThen add 8,844: 1,185,518,129 +8,844 =1,185,526,973.\n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer is correct. Therefore, the sum is 1,185,526,973.\n"] 85%|########4 | 424/500 [10:14:37<1:55:48, 91.43s/it]
