xt (billions) place.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits to add beyond the hundred millions place, the carryover 1 becomes the digit in the billions place. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we have written: 1,045,996,945.\n\nWait, let me confirm this with another method. Maybe adding the numbers using another approach, like breaking them into parts.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using calculator-style addition:.\n\n333,635,842 + 712,334,103.\n\nLet me add the millions first:.\n\n333,635,842 is 333,635,842.\n\n712,334,103 is 712,334,103.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nLet's see, 333 million plus 712 million is 1,045 million. Then the rest:.\n\n635,842 + 334,103 = ?.\n\n635,842 + 334,103:.\n\n600,000 + 300,000 = 900,000.\n\n35,842 + 34,103 = 69,945 (Wait, 35,842 + 34,103: 35,000 +34,000=69,000; 842+103=945. Total 69,945).\n\nSo total of those two parts: 900,000 + 69,945 = 969,945. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
