ws, starting from the right:.\n\nPositions (from right to left):.\n\n1: ones.\n\n2: tens.\n\n3: hundreds.\n\n4: thousands.\n\n5: ten thousands.\n\n6: hundred thousands.\n\n7: millions.\n\n8: ten millions.\n\n9: hundred millions.\n\nSo, column9 is the hundred millions place.\n\nSo when we get to column9 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number's digit: 6 (hundred millions place).\n\nSecond number's digit:4 (hundred millions).\n\nAdding those gives 6+4=10, plus the carryover from column8 (which is ten millions place).\n\nWait, column8 (ten millions):.\n\nFirst number's ten millions digit is 6, second is 4. Their sum is 6+4=10, so we write 0 and carryover1 to column9.\n\nTherefore, when adding column9, it's 6+4 + the carryover1 from column8, so total 10 +1=11. So 11. So we write 1 in the hundred millions place and carryover1 to the next (which is a new digit beyond hundred millions, so we add a 1 at the beginning).\n\nTherefore, the total sum is:.\n\n1 (the carryover) followed by the digits from each column:.\n\nColumn9 result:1 (since 11, so digit is 1 and carryover1).\n\nColumn8:0.\n\nColumn7:8 (from millions place:7+0 + any carryover?).\n\nWait let's step back again, perhaps this is getting confusing. Let me try to do the addition step by step, writing down each digit and carryover:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:1+8=9. Write 9. Carryover 0.\n\nTens:7+0=7. Write7. Carryover0.\n\nHundreds:1+6=7. Write7. Carryover0.\n\nThousands:9+5=14. Write4. Carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:8+3=11 +1=12. Write2. Carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:6+6=12 +1=13. Write3. Carryover1.\n\nMillions:7+0=7 +1=8. Write8. Carryover0.\n\nTen millions:6+4=10. Write0. Carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:6+4=10 +1 (from carryover) =11. Write1. Carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover1 after the hundred millions place, we add that as a new digit to the left. So the total is:.\n\n1 (carryover) followed by the digits from the previous steps.\n\nSo the digits from left to right:.\n\n1 (carryover)