it, let me check the original numbers again. Wait, 954,916,472 is 9 hundred millions, 5 ten millions, 4 millions.. and the second number is 301,905,667 which is 3 hundred millions, 0 ten millions, 1 million.. So the hundred-millions digits are 9 and 3, adding to 12. That's correct. So we have to carry over 1 to the billions place. But since there are no digits beyond that, the carried 1 becomes a 1 in the billions place. So the total sum would have a 1 in the billions place, then 2 in the hundred millions, etc.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:9, tens:3, hundreds:0, thousands:3, ten-thousands:2, hundred-thousands:4, millions:6, ten-millions:5, hundred-millions:2, and billions:1. Wait, let me recount the places step by step to make sure I didn't misalign anything.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more systematically. Let me try again.\n\nLet me align the numbers properly:.\n\n       954,916,472.\n     + 301,905,667.\n     ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n2 + 7 = 9 → Ones: 9.\n\n7 (tens) + 6 (tens) = 13 → Tens: 3, carryover 1.\n\n4 (hundreds) + 5 (hundreds) + 1 = 10 → Hundreds:0, carryover 1.\n\n6 (thousands) + 6 (thousands) +1 =13 → Thousands:3, carryover1.\n\n1 (ten thousands) +0 (ten thousands) +1=2 → Ten thousands:2, no carryover.\n\n9 (hundred thousands) +5 (hundred thousands)=14 → Hundred thousands:4, carryover1.\n\n4 (millions) +1 (millions) +1=6 → Millions:6, no carryover.\n\n5 (ten millions) +0 (ten millions)=5 → Ten millions:5.\n\n9 (hundred millions) +3 (hundred millions)=12 → Hundred millions:2, carryover1.\n\nFinally, the billions place: 0 (since neither number has a digit there except the carryover) → 1.\n\nSo putting all the digits together:.\n\nBillions:1, Hundred millions:2, Ten millions:5, Millions:6, Hundred thousands:4, Ten thousands:2, Thousands:3, Hundreds:0, Tens:3, Ones:9. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
