ver) =6. Write6, no carryover.\n\nPosition7:2 (first) +6 (second)=8. Write8.\n\nPosition8:4 (first) +3 (second)=7. Write7.\n\nPosition9:1 (first) +5 (second)=6. Write6.\n\nPutting all together from position9 to 1: 6 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands?), wait let me check:.\n\nWait the digits we got are:.\n\nPosition9:6 (hundred millions).\n\nPosition8:7 (ten millions).\n\nPosition7:8 (millions).\n\nPosition6:6 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition5:0 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition4:6 (thousands).\n\nPosition3:1 (hundreds).\n\nPosition2:6 (tens).\n\nPosition1:3 (ones).\n\nSo combining these digits:.\n\n6 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
