ons),0 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),8 (hundreds),9 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the digit breakdown earlier.\n\nWait, let me parse the first number again properly.\n\n142,023,890.\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nStarting from the left:\n\nDigit 1 (hundred millions place):1.\n\nDigit 2 (ten millions):4.\n\nDigit3 (millions):2.\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):0.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nDigit6 (thousands):3.\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):8.\n\nDigit8 (tens):9.\n\nDigit9 (ones):0.\n\nWait, but that's left to right. But when adding, we need to go from right to left (ones to higher places).\n\nSo the digits from right (position1 to 9):\n\nPosition1 (ones):0.\n\nPosition2 (tens):9.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):8.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):3.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):2.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):4.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):1.\n\nSecond number:536,582,273.\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\nDigit1 (hundred millions):5.\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):3.\n\nDigit3 (millions):6.\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):8.\n\nDigit6 (thousands):2.\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):2.\n\nDigit8 (tens):7.\n\nDigit9 (ones):3.\n\nSo from right to left:\n\nPosition1 (ones):3.\n\nPosition2 (tens):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):8.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):6.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nNow, let's add each position:\n\nPosition1:0+3=3.\n\nPosition2:9+7=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:8+2=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:3+2=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nPosition5:2+8=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition6:0+5=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nPosition7:2 (first) +6 (second)=8 →8.\n\nPosition8:4+3=7 →7.\n\nPosition9:1+5=6 →6.\n\nSo combining all digits from position9 to position1:6 7 8 6 0 6 1 6 3 → 678,606,163. That's consistent. So the answer is correct.\n"]
