 6, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 + 4 = 9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: 7 + 0 = 7, plus 1 is 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nTen millions place: 6 + 8 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nHundred millions place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 is 10. So write 0 and carry 1. But since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
