      "text": "1,190,323,075? Wait, no. Maybe I need to do it properly.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n          831,100,114\n\n        + 359,223,061\n\n        ----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes:4 +1 =5\n\nTens:1 +0 =1\n\nHundreds:1 +3 =4\n\nThousands:0 +2 =2\n\nTen thousands:0 +2 =2\n\nHundred thousands:1 +2 =3\n\nMillions place:1 (from first number) +9 (from second number) =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions:3 +5 +1 (carryover) =9.\n\nHundred millions:8 +3 =11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1.\n\nBillions place: carryover 1.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:3,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nTens:1,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTherefore the number is 1,190,322,415.\n\nWait, but when I broke it down earlier, adding 831M and 359M:\n\n831,100,114 + 359,223,061 = ?\n\nLet me compute 831,100,114 + 359,223,061:\n\nAdd the millions first: 831,000,000 + 359,000,000 = 1,190,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 100,114 + 223,061 = 323,175.\n\nSo total is 1,190,000,000 + 323,175 = 1,190,323,175.\n\nWait, this contradicts the previous result. Hmm, so now I must have made a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let me check that again.\n\nWait, the first number is 831,100,114. Breaking down:\n\n831,100,114 = 800,000,000 + 31,000,000 + 100,000 + 114.\n\nSecond number: 359,223,061 = 300,000,000 + 59,000,000 + 223,000 + 61.\n\nAdding the parts:\n\n800M + 300M = 1,100M.\n\n31M +59M =90M. Total so far 1,190M.\n\n100,000 +223,000=323,000.\n\n114 +61=175.\n\nSo total is 1,190,000,000 + 323,000 + 175 =1,190,323,175.\n\nAh, so this is different from the digit-wise addition. There must be an error in one of the methods. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's do the digit-wise addition again carefully:\n\nFirst number: 8 3 1 1 0 0 1 1 4\n\nSecond number: 3 5 9 2 2 2 3 0 1\n\nAdding each column from right (ones):\n\nColumn 1 (ones):4+1=5\n\nColumn 2 (tens):1+0=1\n\nColumn3 (hundreds):1+3=4\n\nColumn4 (thousands):0+2=2\n\nColumn5 (ten thousands):0+2=2\n\nColumn6 (hundred thousands):1+2=3\n\nColumn7 (millions):1+9=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\nColumn8 (ten millions):3+5 +1 (carryover)=9.\n\nColumn9 (hundred millions):8+3=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1.\n\nColumn10 (billions): carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (ones to billions) are:\n\n5 (ones),1,4,2,2,3,0,9,1,1.\n\nWait, but when written as a number, the highest digit is billions (position 10), then hundred millions (position9), etc.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:3,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nTens:1,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nSo the number is 1,190,322,415.\n\nBut when I broke it down into parts, I got 1,190,323,175. There's a discrepancy here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let me do the breakdown again:\n\nFirst number's remaining parts after 831 million: 100,114.\n\nSecond number's remaining parts after 359 million: 223,061.\n\nAdding those: 100,114 +223,061 = 323,175. Yes, that's correct. So total is 1,190,000,000 +323,175 =1,190,323,175.\n\nBut according to the digit-wise addition, the answer is 1,190,322,415.\n\nHmm, so there's a conflict here. I must have made a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait let me check the breakdown again. The first number is 831,100,114. Breaking into parts:\n\n831,000,000 + 100,114. Wait, no. Wait 831,100,114 is 800,000,000 +31,000,000 + 100,000 + 114. So total is 831,100,114.\n\nSimilarly, the second number is 359,223,061 = 300,000,000 +59,000,000 + 223,000 +61. So 359,223,061.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 831,000,000 +359,000,000 = 1,190,000,000.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 100,114 +223,061 = 323,175. So total is 1,190,323,175.\n\nBut the digit-wise addition gave me 1,190,322,415.\n\nSo which is correct?\n\nWait, let me do the digit-wise addition again step by step with the actual numbers:\n\nFirst number: 831,100,114.\n\nSecond number:359,223,061.\n\nLet me write them down:\n\n          8 3 1 1 0 0 1 1 4\n\n        + 3 5 9 2 2 2 3 0 1\n\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4 +1 =5 \u2192 5\n\nTens:1 +0 =1 \u21921\n\nHundreds:1 +3 =4 \u21924\n\nThousands:0 +2 =2 \u21922\n\nTen thousands:0 +2 =2 \u21922\n\nHundred thousands:1 +2 =3 \u21923\n\nMillions:1 +9 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1 \u21920, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions:3 +5 =8 + carryover 1 \u21929 \u21929.\n\nHundred millions:8 +3 =11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1 \u21921, carryover 1.\n\nBillions: carryover 1 \u21921.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:5,\n\nTens:1,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nHundred thousands:3,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nBillions:1.\n\nSo arranging from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:3,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nTens:1,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nThus the number is 1,190,322,415.\n\nWait, but the breakdown method gave me 1,190,323,175. There's a discrepancy of 760 here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check the breakdown again:\n\nFirst number: 831,100,114.\n\nSecond number:359,223,061.\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nLet me add them digit by digit again using another method:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes:4 +1=5 \u2192 5.\n\nTens:1 +0=1 \u21921.\n\nHundreds:1+3=4 \u21924.\n\nThousands:0+2=2 \u21922.\n\nTen thousands:0+2=2 \u21922.\n\nHundred thousands:1+2=3 \u21923.\n\nMillions:1+9=10 \u21920 with carryover 1.\n\nTen millions:3+5 +1=9 \u21929.\n\nHundred millions:8+3=11 \u21921 with carryover 1.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nSo the total is indeed 1,190,322,415.\n\nWait, but when I broke it down into parts, I added 100,114 and 223,061 as 323,175, but let me verify that:\n\n100,114 +223,061:\n\n100,114 +223,061:\n\nAdd the thousands: 100,000 +223,000 =323,000.\n\nThen the remaining: 114 +61 =175. So total is 323,175. That's correct.\n\nSo 831,100,114 is 831,000,000 + 100,114.\n\n359,223,061 is 359,000,000 +223,061.\n\nAdding 831,000,000 +359,000,000 =1,190,000,000.\n\nAdding 100,114 +223,061 =323,175.\n\nTotal sum:1,190,000,000 +323,175 =1,190,323,175.\n\nWait, but that's conflicting with the digit-wise addition. So where's the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait a second, I think I made an error in the breakdown.\n\nWait the first number is 831,100,114.\n\nBreaking it down as 800,000,000 +31,000,000 +100,000 +114. That's correct.\n\nSecond number:359,223,061 is 300,000,000 +59,000,000 +223,000 +61. Correct.\n\nAdding the millions parts:\n\n800M +300M =1,100M.\n\n31M +59M =90M \u2192 total 1,190M.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n100,000 +223,000 =323,000.\n\n114 +61 =175.\n\nTotal remaining parts:323,000 +175 =323,175.\n\nTotal sum:1,190,000,000 +323,175 =1,190,323,175.\n\nBut digit-wise addition says 1,190,322,415.\n\nHmm, so there's a difference of 760 between the two methods. Let me check the digit-wise again.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the digit positions. Let me write the numbers vertically:\n\n          8 3 1 1 0 0 1 1 4\n\n        + 3 5 9 2 2 2 3 0 1\n\n        ---------------------\n\nLet me write each digit with their positions:\n\nFirst number (831,100,114):\n\nPosition 1 (ones):4\n\nPosition 2 (tens):1\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):0\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1\n\nPosition7 (millions):1\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8\n\nSecond number (359,223,061):\n\nPosition1 (ones):1\n\nPosition2 (tens):0\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2\n\nPosition7 (millions):9\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3\n\nPosition10 (billions):0 (since it's a 9-digit number).\n\nWait, actually, the second number is 359,223,061 which is 9 digits, so:\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3,\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5,\n\nPosition7 (millions):9,\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2,\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2,\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2,\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3,\n\nPosition2 (tens):0,\n\nPosition1 (ones):1.\n\nWait, so let me list each position properly:\n\nLet me write each digit from position1 (ones) to position9 (hundred millions) for both numbers.\n\nFirst number:\n\nPosition1:4\n\nPosition2:1\n\nPosition3:1\n\nPosition4:0\n\nPosition5:0\n\nPosition6:1\n\nPosition7:1\n\nPosition8:3\n\nPosition9:8\n\nSecond number:\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition2:0\n\nPosition3:3\n\nPosition4:2\n\nPosition5:2\n\nPosition6:2\n\nPosition7:9\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition9:3\n\nAdding each position:\n\nPosition1:4+1=5\n\nPosition2:1+0=1\n\nPosition3:1+3=4\n\nPosition4:0+2=2\n\nPosition5:0+2=2\n\nPosition6:1+2=3\n\nPosition7:1+9=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover1\n\nPosition8:3+5 +1(carry)=9\n\nPosition9:8+3=11 \u2192 write1, carryover1\n\nPosition10: carryover1.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to position10 are:\n\nPosition10:1,\n\nPosition9:1,\n\nPosition8:9,\n\nPosition7:0,\n\nPosition6:3,\n\nPosition5:2,\n\nPosition4:2,\n\nPosition3:4,\n\nPosition2:1,\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nSo arranging from highest to lowest (position10 to position1):\n\n1 (position10),\n\n1 (position9),\n\n9 (position8),\n\n0 (position7),\n\n3 (position6),\n\n2 (position5),\n\n2 (position4),\n\n4 (position3),\n\n1 (position2),\n\n5 (position1).\n\nThus the number is 1 1 9 0 3 2 2 4 1 5 \u2192 1,190,322,415.\n\nAh, so the breakdown method must be wrong. Let me check again:\n\nWait, in the breakdown approach, I considered the first number as 831,000,000 +100,114. But 831,000,000 +100,114 is 831,100,114. Correct.\n\nSecond number is 359,000,000 +223,061 =359,223,061. Correct.\n\nAdding 831,000,000 +359,000,000 =1,190,000,000. Correct.\n\nAdding 100,114 +223,061:\n\n100,114 +223,061:\n\nLet me compute 100,114 +223,061 step by step.\n\n100,114 +200,000 =300,114.\n\n300,114 +23,061 =323,175. Yes, that's correct. So total is 1,190,323,175.\n\nBut according to digit-wise addition, it's 1,190,322,415.\n\nWait, so there's a discrepancy of 760. 1,190,323,175 -1,190,322,415 =760.\n\nHmm, so which is correct? Let me do a manual addition of the two numbers:\n\nLet me write the numbers:\n\nFirst number: 831,100,114\n\nSecond number:359,223,061\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4 +1 =5 (ones)\n\n1 +0=1 (tens)\n\n1 +3=4 (hundreds)\n\n0 +2=2 (thousands)\n\n0 +2=2 (ten thousands)\n\n1 +2=3 (hundred thousands)\n\n1 +9=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1 (millions)\n\n3 (ten millions) +5 (ten millions from second number) +1 (carryover) =9 (ten millions)\n\n8 (hundred millions) +3 (hundred millions from second number)=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover1 (hundred millions place)\n\nBillions: carryover1 \u21921.\n\nSo the total is 1,190,322,415.\n\nWait, but why does the breakdown method give a different result?\n\nAh! Wait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown's addition of the smaller parts. Let me check the smaller parts again:\n\nFirst number's remaining part after 831 million: 100,114.\n\nSecond number's remaining part after 359 million: 223,061.\n\nAdding these two: 100,114 +223,061.\n\nLet me do this addition step by step:\n\n100,114\n\n+223,061\n\n------------\n\nAdding ones:4+1=5\n\nTens:1+6=7 \u2192 wait, wait, no, wait:\n\nWait, the second number's breakdown: 223,061 is 223,000 +61, but when adding 100,114 +223,061:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n  100,114\n\n+223,061\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4+1=5\n\nTens:1+6=7 (because 0 in the first number's tens place? Wait, no:\n\nWait, the first number is 100,114:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n100,114 is 1 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),1 (hundreds),1 (tens),4 (ones).\n\nWait, no, 100,114 is:\n\n100,114:\n\n1 (hundred thousands),\n\n0 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n1 (hundreds),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n4 (ones).\n\nSecond number's