imately 110 million plus 874 thousand plus 933.\n\n475,219,168 is 475 million plus 219 thousand plus 168.\n\nAdding the millions: 110 + 475 = 585 million.\n\nAdding the thousands: 874,933 + 219,168. Let's compute that:\n\n874,933 + 200,000 = 1,074,933\n\nThen add 19,168: 1,074,933 + 19,168 = 1,094,101.\n\nSo total is 585,000,000 + 1,094,101 = 586,094,101. Okay, so that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 586,094,101. I think that's right. I should make sure that in the digit-by-digit addition, each step was correct. Let me go through once more quickly:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:3+8=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:3+6+1=10 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:9+1+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:4+9+1=14 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands:7+1+1=9 \u2714\ufe0f (Wait, 7 from first number, 1 from second, plus carryover 1? Wait, the carryover from thousands place was 1, but in thousands place, 4+9=13 plus carryover 1 makes 14, so carryover 1 to the next (ten-thousands place). So in ten-thousands place: first number's digit is 7, second is 1, plus carryover 1, so 7+1+1=9. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands place: first number's 8 and second's 2, so 8+2=10, plus any carryover? Wait, the carryover from the ten-thousands place was none, since 7+1+1=9. So 8+2=10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: first has 0, second has 5, plus carryover 1: 0+5+1=6. Correct.\n\nTen-millions place: first's 1 and second's7. 1+7=8.\n\nHundred-millions: 1+4=5.\n\nYes, all steps check out. So the final answer is indeed 586,094,101.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 110,874,933 and 475,219,168 is \\boxed{586094101}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 110874933 and 475219168?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 3 (from 110874933) + 8 (from 475219168) = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n2. The tens place: 3 (from 110874933) + 6 (from 475219168) + 1 (carryover) = 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n3. The hundreds place: 9 (from 110874933)