o we note 4 here and carry over 1.\n\nNext is the ten millions place. The first number has a 7 and the second has a 7. 7 + 7 = 14, plus the carried 1 gives 15. So we put 5 in this place and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred millions place. The first number has a 1 and the second has a 2. 1 + 2 = 3, plus the carried 1 equals 4. So that's the last digit. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
