.\n\nAdding the millions parts:\n\n174,000,000 + 279,000,000 = 453,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n641,570 + 819,878.\n\nCalculating that: 641,570 + 800,000 = 1,441,570. Then subtract the overcount? Wait, no. Let's do it properly.\n\n641,570 + 819,878:\n\n641,570 + 800,000 = 1,441,570.\n\nThen add 19,878: 1,441,570 + 19,878 = 1,461,448.\n\nSo total sum is 453,000,000 + 1,461,448 = 454,461,448. Okay, that matches the previous result. So I think that's correct. Therefore, the final answer should be 454,461,448.\n"]
