wer is 1,189,603,991.\n\nBut let me check once more using another method, perhaps adding digit by digit again carefully.\n\nLet me write the two numbers vertically aligned:\n\n          3 9 5 5 2 0 9 8 3\n\n        + 7 9 4 0 8 3 0 0 8\n\n        ----------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n3 +8 =11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTens:8 +0 +1=9 →9.\n\nHundreds:9 +0=9.\n\nThousands:0 +3=3.\n\nTen thousands:2 +8=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +0 +1=6.\n\nMillions:5 +4=9.\n\nTen millions:9 +9=18 →8, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:3 +7 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThe carryover1 becomes the billions digit.\n\nSo the result is 1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),9 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),9 (hundreds),9 (tens),1 (ones).\n\nThus, the number is 1,189,603,991. That seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 1,189,603,991.\n\nBut let me check with a calculator for confirmation.\n\nCalculating 395,520,983 +794,083,008.\n\n395,520,983 +794,083,008 = ?\n\nLet me compute:\n\n395,520,983 + 700,000,000 = 1,095,520,983.\n\nAdding 94,083,008 to that:\n\n1,095,520,983 + 94,083,008.\n\nFirst add 94,000,000: 1,095,520,983 +94,000,000 = 1,189,520,983.\n\nThen add 83,008: 1,189,520,983 +83,008 = 1,189,603,991. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the answer is indeed 1,189,603,991.\n\nTherefore, the initial mistake was in the hundreds place calculation where I incorrectly added the thousands digit instead. But after correcting that, the result is accurate.\n"]
