tion 2 (tens):9\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):4\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):9\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):8\n\nPosition 7 (millions):4\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):8\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):6\n\nSimilarly, the second number 993,616,165:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):5\n\nPosition 2 (tens):6\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):6\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):1\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):6\n\nPosition 7 (millions):3\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):9\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):9\n\nSo adding each position:\n\nPosition 1: 1+5=6\n\nPosition 2:9+6=15 →5 carry 1\n\nPosition3:4+1=5 +1=6\n\nPosition4:9 (first) +6 (second) =15 →5 carry1\n\nPosition5:6+1=7 +1=8\n\nPosition6:8+6=14 →4 carry1\n\nPosition7:4+3=7 +1=8\n\nPosition8:8+9=17 →7 carry1\n\nPosition9:6+9=15 +1=16 →6 carry1\n\nNow, the carryover 1 from position9 goes to a new position10 (billions place).\n\nSo the total sum is:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:7\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:5\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:6\n\nWait, putting all together:\n\nBillions (1), Hundred millions (6), Ten millions (7), Millions (8), Hundred thousands (4), Ten thousands (8), Thousands (5), Hundreds (6), Tens (5), Ones (6).\n\nWait, so the number is 1,678,485,656?\n\nWait let's construct it step by step:\n\nStarting from the billions place:\n\n1 (billions)\n\nThen hundred millions:6 → making it 1,600,000,000\n\nThen ten millions:7 → 1,670,000,000\n\nMillions:8 → 1,678,000,000\n\nHundred thousands:4 → 1,678,400,000\n\nTen thousands:8 → 1,678,480,000\n\nThousands:5 →1,678,485,000\n\nHundreds:6 →1,678,485,600\n\nTens:5 →1,678,485,650\n\nOnes:6 →1,678,485,656\n\nYes, that seems right. So the final sum is 1,678,485,656.\n\nWait but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 684,869,491 + 993,616,165.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n684,869,491 is 684 million plus 869,491.\n\n993,616,165 is 993 million plus 616,165.\n\nAdding the millions: 684 + 993 = 1,677 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 869,491 + 616,165.\n\nCalculating 869,491 + 616,165:\n\n800,000 + 600,000 =1,400,000\n\n69,491 +16,165= 85,656.\n\nSo total is 1,400,000 +85,656 =1,485,656.\n\nAdding to the 1,677 million:\n\n1,677,000,000 +1,485,656 =1,678,485,656. Same result. Okay, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,678,485,656.\n"] 99%|#########8| 494/500 [12:15:34<10:11, 101.91s/it]
